WEBVTT

00:16.224 --> 00:18.476
Go easy on the driving today.

00:19.144 --> 00:22.689
Traffic laws? Yeah, right.
We break every other rule out there.

00:22.772 --> 00:23.982
What rules did we break?

00:24.774 --> 00:26.901
What do you think?
The rules in the killing industry.

00:27.444 --> 00:29.821
We must only work
on company-sanctioned shows.

00:29.904 --> 00:31.531
We can't even kill a minor.

00:31.614 --> 00:33.783
These fucking rules, I swear.

00:34.868 --> 00:36.369
What pisses me off the most is

00:36.453 --> 00:39.039
that the rules were made
by MK's chairman, Cha Min-kyu,

00:39.122 --> 00:40.999
the top dog in the business.

00:41.499 --> 00:45.086
Unemployed, no affiliation.
How the hell are we gonna make a living?

00:45.587 --> 00:47.964
I hate the word "unemployed."

00:48.465 --> 00:51.718
Fuck, just talking about him
makes me wanna off the guy.

00:52.218 --> 00:56.222
What do you say? Should I just send
a bloody knife to Cha Min-kyu?

00:57.140 --> 00:58.433
Do you have a death wish?

00:59.350 --> 01:01.978
To take on Cha Min-kyu in a death match,

01:02.062 --> 01:03.438
you'd need to be Gil Boksoon

01:03.521 --> 01:07.025
or that hotshot from MK
with the insect name, Ma…

01:07.525 --> 01:08.777
Who was that kid again?

01:08.860 --> 01:13.656
MANTIS

01:14.324 --> 01:16.743
We gotta pull in as much cash as we can.

01:16.826 --> 01:19.370
It's not like we've got
a pension waiting for us.

01:19.454 --> 01:21.206
Hey, at least we're getting by.

01:21.289 --> 01:25.293
These days, a lot of kids are just
loafing around because there's no work.

01:26.961 --> 01:32.467
Kids these days have the wrong mindset.

01:33.009 --> 01:35.303
What do they mean there's no work?

01:35.804 --> 01:39.641
They won't bust their ass,
but they still chase a fat paycheck.

01:39.724 --> 01:43.103
That's a classic contradiction.

01:43.186 --> 01:45.730
That's why people call you a boomer.

01:46.231 --> 01:47.982
Don't blame the kids.

01:48.066 --> 01:50.193
Blame the fucked-up society.

01:50.276 --> 01:52.821
Why place the blame on our society?

01:52.904 --> 01:54.697
It has always been fucked up.

01:54.781 --> 01:58.159
Fair enough. Kids can't even score a job,

01:58.243 --> 02:01.412
and guys our age gotta bust our asses
working two jobs just to survive.

02:01.496 --> 02:04.124
Hit your fifties,
and they start pushing you to retire.

02:04.207 --> 02:06.292
Shit's really fucked up.

02:07.127 --> 02:08.378
Yeah.

02:08.461 --> 02:11.714
That's why we're stuck
in a messed-up life like this.

02:20.807 --> 02:22.058
Where are you going?

02:22.559 --> 02:23.685
Bathroom.

02:24.435 --> 02:26.813
We're running late. Hurry.

02:38.700 --> 02:40.201
For the love of…

02:41.452 --> 02:45.707
Would it have killed him
to do the job properly?

03:15.028 --> 03:15.904
First,

03:16.404 --> 03:19.240
you must not kill minors.

03:20.074 --> 03:20.909
Second,

03:21.409 --> 03:23.953
you will only take on shows
sanctioned by your company.

03:24.746 --> 03:25.580
Third…

03:29.375 --> 03:32.670
you must always attempt shows
sanctioned by your company.

03:35.256 --> 03:38.426
MK made those rules.

03:39.427 --> 03:43.223
Unemployed people like us
can't even afford to play by them.

03:45.350 --> 03:46.517
Not at all.

03:47.185 --> 03:51.022
I'm sure a lot of companies
sought out men of your talent.

03:52.815 --> 03:56.361
Any company that's not MK in this game

03:56.444 --> 03:58.655
isn't really worth it these days, is it?

04:02.700 --> 04:04.244
My brother…

04:06.204 --> 04:08.289
Was his death quick and painless?

04:09.499 --> 04:10.875
I'm sure it was.

04:11.417 --> 04:12.669
Your brother

04:13.628 --> 04:15.380
didn't put up much of a fight.

04:34.857 --> 04:37.568
If you go that way,
things will be very painful.

04:48.079 --> 04:50.748
Who… the heck are you?

04:55.837 --> 04:57.630
What took you so long?

05:03.928 --> 05:05.096
I waited forever.

05:08.558 --> 05:09.726
I see.

05:11.394 --> 05:13.229
Sickles in both hands.

05:13.730 --> 05:16.482
You must be the hotshot
making waves lately.

05:17.233 --> 05:18.651
Grasshopper, was it?

05:25.366 --> 05:27.368
What was it? Was it Ma…

05:28.036 --> 05:29.620
What was it again?

05:29.704 --> 05:30.621
Right, Maggot!

05:30.705 --> 05:32.123
Are you kidding me?

05:33.458 --> 05:35.460
It's Mantis, you bastard.

05:36.085 --> 05:38.838
AKA the Death Demon,
in case you don't know.

05:40.089 --> 05:41.841
"Bastard" right off the bat?

05:41.924 --> 05:43.843
Should I loop in your parents?

05:43.926 --> 05:45.345
Well, this is great.

05:45.845 --> 05:48.431
I've been dying to see you myself.

05:48.514 --> 05:49.390
Me?

05:50.516 --> 05:51.351
Min-kyu.

05:53.019 --> 05:55.855
I guess this geezer fears you
but thinks he can take me on.

05:55.938 --> 05:57.106
Either way,

05:57.690 --> 06:00.777
I guess my brother and I
still have an A ranking,

06:00.860 --> 06:04.280
seeing how you showed up in person
with your Mantis sidekick.

06:04.364 --> 06:06.574
Don't get full of yourself, you geezer.

06:07.533 --> 06:08.868
The chairman is only here

06:08.951 --> 06:11.162
because I had something to tell him
before my vacation.

06:11.245 --> 06:13.790
I know you were late on purpose
to make me do the work.

06:14.457 --> 06:15.750
Go do your thing.

06:16.250 --> 06:17.251
I'm off.

06:17.835 --> 06:19.712
We need to talk. Where are you going?

06:19.796 --> 06:22.215
Go sit and rest.
I'll wrap this up quickly, okay?

06:22.715 --> 06:23.716
Just sit and wait!

06:58.668 --> 07:00.128
That was solid, kid.

07:44.964 --> 07:47.049
Good job, Maggot!

07:48.301 --> 07:50.136
I told you. I'm not Maggot.

07:50.219 --> 07:53.764
Hello, please bring
two more cleaners with you.

07:53.848 --> 07:55.558
It's Mantis's work,

07:56.559 --> 07:57.810
so it's a bit messy.

07:57.894 --> 07:58.728
Right.

08:00.396 --> 08:02.315
Cut to the chase. I really need to go.

08:03.149 --> 08:06.486
I just wanted to ask you
to let me out of my contract.

08:07.111 --> 08:09.739
Come on, we both know
a seven-year deal is a stretch,

08:09.822 --> 08:11.407
considering my brand value.

08:11.491 --> 08:13.075
Do you want to join another company?

08:13.659 --> 08:15.912
Or are you starting something yourself?

08:16.704 --> 08:17.622
Well…

08:18.122 --> 08:19.207
Is this about

08:20.458 --> 08:22.168
that friend of yours again?

08:23.711 --> 08:26.214
You know, it's not exactly that, but…

08:27.965 --> 08:30.801
Enjoy your vacation, okay?

08:36.390 --> 08:37.558
Min-kyu, wait.

08:39.060 --> 08:40.061
What now?

08:48.694 --> 08:50.238
What is the meaning of this?

08:50.821 --> 08:52.073
It's a bloody knife.

08:53.449 --> 08:54.784
Oh, a sickle doesn't count?

09:07.338 --> 09:08.297
Hold on.

09:11.050 --> 09:13.511
You were actually going to take it?

09:13.594 --> 09:16.430
Come on, it was just a joke.

09:16.931 --> 09:20.601
I was kidding. Why take it so seriously?

09:29.694 --> 09:31.112
I will enjoy my vacation, then.

09:34.907 --> 09:36.993
You're not ready to be independent.

09:37.076 --> 09:39.829
Strong negotiation skills are key
to running a business.

09:39.912 --> 09:42.707
Come on,
I put my life on the line this time.

09:42.790 --> 09:45.543
I know, and it almost worked this time.

09:45.626 --> 09:46.460
Huh?

09:47.503 --> 09:48.504
For real?

09:49.005 --> 09:51.215
Then what? Should I offer it again?

09:54.802 --> 09:55.761
I guess not.

09:58.097 --> 09:59.890
Let's redo the contract when you return.

10:00.766 --> 10:02.685
And set up an interview for your friend.

10:02.768 --> 10:04.312
Whoa, seriously?

10:04.812 --> 10:06.564
No way! Chairman?

10:07.064 --> 10:09.984
You'd better not go back on that later.

10:10.484 --> 10:11.652
Holy crap.

10:11.736 --> 10:14.572
Chairman Cha.
You'd better keep your promise.

10:15.197 --> 10:16.741
All hail Cha Min-kyu!

10:17.241 --> 10:19.118
Let's go, MK!

10:21.203 --> 10:23.956
Hey, didn't I tell you to just trust me?

10:24.040 --> 10:26.250
You're also working for MK now.

10:27.001 --> 10:29.795
Get that body in shape while I'm away.

10:31.672 --> 10:33.090
What are you talking about?

10:33.174 --> 10:35.468
MK was perfectly fine.
Why would it go under?

10:35.551 --> 10:37.720
What? Say that again. What about Min-kyu?

10:37.803 --> 10:38.929
Min-kyu is dead?

10:39.430 --> 10:40.640
Seriously?

10:41.474 --> 10:42.725
Boksoon did him in?

10:45.686 --> 10:46.604
I'm hella jealous.

10:46.687 --> 10:49.482
If I had seen this coming,
I would've taken him out back then.

10:49.565 --> 10:52.360
Where are you anyway? I don't see you.

10:52.443 --> 10:54.236
Where else? I'm working.

10:54.320 --> 10:56.447
Come on, we haven't hung out in forever.

10:56.530 --> 10:57.865
MURDER SUSPECT WANTED

10:57.948 --> 10:59.575
I'm busy making ends meet.

11:01.285 --> 11:02.536
I have to go now.

11:06.040 --> 11:09.710
Of course, work comes first.
Go get it done.

11:10.211 --> 11:13.464
Go on, work hard,
and pocket everything without me.

11:13.547 --> 11:15.675
-There he is!
-What's with the crowd?

11:15.758 --> 11:16.676
Oh, right.

11:16.759 --> 11:20.388
Now that MK's down,
I hear the other companies are after you.

11:20.471 --> 11:22.640
-Mantis!
-You're the Mantis, right?

11:22.723 --> 11:23.683
We're from Yujin.

11:23.766 --> 11:25.059
Mantis, you know me, right?

11:25.142 --> 11:26.143
Please come with us.

11:26.227 --> 11:27.812
-Sorry, guys.
-We'll treat you well.

11:27.895 --> 11:29.980
-I'm sorry.
-Our company's better.

11:30.564 --> 11:31.649
Have fun.

11:35.695 --> 11:36.570
That's hot.

11:39.115 --> 11:40.116
Now…

11:40.950 --> 11:42.702
I'm back.

11:42.785 --> 11:44.328
Good work out there.

11:44.412 --> 11:46.247
That smells amazing.

11:47.206 --> 11:48.290
Why the galbi-jjim?

11:49.458 --> 11:50.960
I heard Han-ul is back.

11:52.044 --> 11:55.339
Hey, I'm sure he missed Korean food
while he was abroad.

11:56.674 --> 11:59.969
I figured I'd make enough
to share with everyone.

12:00.469 --> 12:02.930
Good grief, boss.

12:03.431 --> 12:07.643
Han-ul would never join us here,
even if MK disappeared into thin air.

12:08.144 --> 12:10.229
I never said he would. Sheesh.

12:10.813 --> 12:11.814
What's this?

12:11.897 --> 12:12.732
EVICTION NOTICE

12:13.566 --> 12:14.525
Oh, that?

12:15.025 --> 12:16.986
They want us out of the office next month.

12:17.987 --> 12:20.239
I guess I'll have to go back to fieldwork.

12:20.322 --> 12:22.283
You're not even well.

12:22.783 --> 12:25.369
I'll take more shows.
Just bring me whatever you can.

12:25.453 --> 12:26.871
I'm sorry.

12:27.788 --> 12:29.623
You deserve better than this.

12:30.124 --> 12:32.376
I would've been unemployed

12:32.460 --> 12:35.212
if you hadn't taken me in
after I ruined my company.

12:35.838 --> 12:37.590
Holy fuck!

12:38.674 --> 12:40.843
Hasn't the elevator been fixed yet?

12:41.510 --> 12:44.180
What are you wearing?
Is that European style?

12:44.263 --> 12:45.639
Sharp eyes.

12:46.140 --> 12:48.726
It's the latest drop.
I bet you're hella jealous.

12:48.809 --> 12:50.686
-Mantis, have you been well?
-Yes.

12:50.770 --> 12:52.438
Hey, it's been forever, and you…

12:52.521 --> 12:53.355
What's that smell?

12:53.439 --> 12:55.191
The boss made galbi-jjim

12:55.274 --> 12:57.526
because your dumb ass was coming.

12:57.610 --> 12:59.695
Whoa, galbi-jjim?

12:59.779 --> 13:02.573
I had tons. Korean restaurants
are everywhere in Europe.

13:02.656 --> 13:03.491
Oh, right.

13:03.574 --> 13:05.159
Let's go. The kids are waiting.

13:05.242 --> 13:06.869
-Hey!
-Can I leave this with you?

13:06.952 --> 13:08.829
Of course you can.

13:09.622 --> 13:10.790
Come on!

13:12.958 --> 13:13.918
Get going.

13:15.252 --> 13:16.295
I'll be right back.

13:23.969 --> 13:25.596
Yeah, drink up!

13:32.228 --> 13:33.729
We're not taking customers today.

13:33.813 --> 13:36.232
Open up before I kill you.

13:36.315 --> 13:39.193
He doesn't want more customers.
He hates crowds.

13:39.276 --> 13:41.028
Which prick said that?

13:41.111 --> 13:43.489
Mantis. You still want to come in?

13:43.572 --> 13:45.449
Nah, I'm good.

13:46.992 --> 13:48.536
That's not it.

13:53.582 --> 13:56.627
Jae-yi was just about to rejoin MK.

13:56.710 --> 13:58.754
What's she going to do now?

14:01.257 --> 14:04.677
Why do you sound so bummed about it?

14:04.760 --> 14:08.264
Come on, bro.
Once Jae-yi gets in, we'd be next in line.

14:08.347 --> 14:10.015
You think we're equals, huh?

14:10.099 --> 14:11.058
-Suit yourself!
-Hey!

14:11.141 --> 14:12.893
-Don't.
-Why not make me your minion?

14:12.977 --> 14:14.812
What, you think his head's a drum?

14:14.895 --> 14:16.564
At least pay him before you hit him.

14:17.273 --> 14:18.440
Hey.

14:19.441 --> 14:23.612
Did the rest of you think you'd be next
once Jae-yi joined MK too?

14:24.113 --> 14:25.197
Yes.

14:25.281 --> 14:27.950
Look at these punks.
You gotta be kidding me.

14:28.450 --> 14:29.368
Hey!

14:30.452 --> 14:31.954
Do I owe you something or what?

14:32.037 --> 14:34.415
Su-min, why aren't you saying anything?

14:34.498 --> 14:35.374
What do you mean?

14:35.457 --> 14:36.709
When he wasn't around,

14:36.792 --> 14:39.295
you said we should
start a company with Jae-yi.

14:39.378 --> 14:40.880
Start another company?

14:40.963 --> 14:42.172
It was just an idea.

14:42.256 --> 14:43.299
Why not?

14:43.382 --> 14:44.383
We have you.

14:44.466 --> 14:47.344
That's right. With your reputation,
it's totally possible.

14:48.971 --> 14:50.014
-It's possible.
-See?

14:50.097 --> 14:51.098
But…

14:51.181 --> 14:53.350
The boomers are getting
absolutely wrecked.

14:53.434 --> 14:54.977
This is our chance.

14:55.060 --> 14:58.689
He may be good at killing,
but business is a different ball game.

14:58.772 --> 15:00.524
-You stay out of this.
-Well…

15:00.608 --> 15:03.193
I'm just saying that someone like Jae-yi
should be in charge.

15:03.277 --> 15:05.571
Diligent, responsible,
and doesn't beat us up.

15:05.654 --> 15:07.072
You little punks.

15:07.156 --> 15:09.742
I said I'd take care of Jae-yi,
not you guys.

15:09.825 --> 15:11.785
Hey, why would you take care of me?

15:12.286 --> 15:13.120
Huh?

15:13.704 --> 15:16.373
Did I ever ask you to get me into MK?

15:18.167 --> 15:19.251
She's right.

15:19.335 --> 15:21.962
You shouldn't say you'll take care of
a woman who's already taken.

15:22.963 --> 15:24.381
Taken? What do you mean?

15:25.507 --> 15:26.342
Wait.

15:27.551 --> 15:28.594
Are you seeing someone?

15:29.094 --> 15:30.346
Holy crap.

15:30.888 --> 15:31.722
That's great.

15:31.805 --> 15:33.849
Wow, so you're seeing someone, huh?

15:33.933 --> 15:35.351
Hey, congrats.

15:38.020 --> 15:39.563
I'm gonna hit the bathroom.

15:39.647 --> 15:40.773
Hey, you idiot.

15:41.649 --> 15:43.859
-Read the room.
-What?

15:49.073 --> 15:50.032
Hey!

15:51.742 --> 15:54.787
You think starting a company
is child's play?

15:55.287 --> 15:56.997
Why would I take care of you?

15:57.081 --> 15:59.041
Because you just don't have the skills.

15:59.124 --> 16:00.542
-What?
-Neither do we.

16:00.626 --> 16:02.002
Good for you, dipshit!

16:02.711 --> 16:05.047
So you think I don't have the skills?

16:05.130 --> 16:06.256
That's right.

16:07.758 --> 16:09.802
We're tied at eight right now.

16:09.885 --> 16:11.887
You actually kept track of that?

16:12.388 --> 16:14.431
Technically, isn't it nine to seven?

16:14.515 --> 16:17.768
I've won nine straight since then.

16:21.689 --> 16:24.191
Do you seriously think
you got me that day?

16:24.274 --> 16:25.859
What, you don't think so?

16:27.444 --> 16:28.278
Damn it.

16:45.504 --> 16:49.508
I swear I heard Jae-yi
definitely took down Mantis that day.

16:50.009 --> 16:53.303
Hey, then why on earth
would MK debut Mantis first?

16:53.387 --> 16:54.972
I'm telling you, it's true.

16:55.055 --> 16:58.308
That's why Jae-yi got pissed and left MK.

16:58.392 --> 17:01.103
Shouldn't someone step in
and stop their fight?

17:03.856 --> 17:04.982
Hey, remember?

17:05.899 --> 17:08.235
-When I lost to you seven times--
-Eight.

17:08.318 --> 17:09.361
Right, seven.

17:10.237 --> 17:13.741
But I didn't get that pissed
every time I lost.

17:15.868 --> 17:17.161
You know why?

17:19.830 --> 17:21.540
Don't read too much into it.

17:23.959 --> 17:25.711
I was just helping you up.

17:39.600 --> 17:40.851
Oh, that's right.

17:40.934 --> 17:43.270
So, what about your boyfriend?

17:43.771 --> 17:45.397
Is he in the industry or a civilian?

17:46.523 --> 17:49.151
I guess dating someone in the industry
gets you nothing.

17:49.234 --> 17:52.362
Does that matter now,
considering even MK is getting wrecked?

17:52.446 --> 17:54.698
Hey, I've told you countless times.

17:54.782 --> 17:56.825
MK is really done for.

17:56.909 --> 17:58.535
All the investors pulled out.

17:58.619 --> 18:00.454
Only puppet executives remain.

18:00.537 --> 18:01.914
They have nothing now.

18:01.997 --> 18:03.415
A company like MK

18:03.499 --> 18:05.084
won't go down that easily.

18:05.167 --> 18:06.001
Get this.

18:06.668 --> 18:08.670
MK's Cha Min-kyu may be dead,

18:08.754 --> 18:10.923
but Cha Min-hee was managing things
under him.

18:11.006 --> 18:14.760
That lady is also dead.
Boksoon did her in.

18:17.262 --> 18:19.973
What the fuck is her problem?

18:20.057 --> 18:24.520
So the startup we talked about
with the others…

18:28.148 --> 18:28.982
Hey.

18:29.900 --> 18:31.151
There is one person.

18:31.235 --> 18:32.152
Who?

18:35.405 --> 18:36.365
Right.

18:38.826 --> 18:39.952
Wanna come along?

19:05.686 --> 19:06.645
Good God.

19:06.728 --> 19:08.647
Dear old man.

19:16.947 --> 19:17.781
Huh?

19:20.784 --> 19:22.828
-It's you, isn't it?
-Yes.

19:24.121 --> 19:25.497
Nice to meet you.

19:27.332 --> 19:28.750
I'm Benjamin Jo.

19:29.251 --> 19:30.919
"Meta Software."

19:34.506 --> 19:35.883
How can I help you?

19:38.135 --> 19:39.803
I'm just a huge fan, Mantis.

19:41.138 --> 19:41.972
Sir.

19:42.598 --> 19:43.849
We're running late.

19:45.809 --> 19:47.686
I have a meeting to get to.

19:48.353 --> 19:49.354
Such a bummer.

19:49.855 --> 19:51.148
Give me a call sometime.

19:57.696 --> 19:59.198
He wants me to call him?

20:04.786 --> 20:05.871
Old man.

20:09.958 --> 20:11.627
It's been a while.

20:12.252 --> 20:14.254
I haven't been in touch, have I?

20:14.338 --> 20:15.672
Well, it was because…

20:15.756 --> 20:17.090
Hold on. Just hear me out.

20:17.174 --> 20:19.009
You haven't called me either!

20:27.643 --> 20:28.477
Old Man Dokgo?

20:29.144 --> 20:31.021
-Mantis went to see him?
-Why?

20:31.104 --> 20:33.565
What's wrong with him
visiting his former teacher?

20:34.149 --> 20:36.693
He was also the one
who gave him the nickname "Mantis."

20:36.777 --> 20:37.778
Right, Jae-yi?

20:37.861 --> 20:38.695
Yeah.

20:38.779 --> 20:39.696
Jealous.

20:39.780 --> 20:43.242
If I had a master like Old Man Dokgo,
I wouldn't be like this now.

20:43.325 --> 20:45.869
-Was that for Jae-yi to hear?
-Why, you…

20:45.953 --> 20:48.538
-I didn't mean…
-It's fine, you punk. Just eat your ribs.

20:48.622 --> 20:51.875
Why didn't you go with him?
You don't even have work today.

20:51.959 --> 20:53.502
I have a date later.

20:55.254 --> 20:59.091
You've really been living the good life,
haven't you?

21:04.179 --> 21:05.681
I wasn't going to touch it.

21:07.474 --> 21:09.017
Wow.

21:10.352 --> 21:12.521
Why on earth
did you even put this stuff here?

21:13.021 --> 21:15.357
Man, this taste of yours.

21:22.739 --> 21:24.449
Damn it.

21:24.533 --> 21:25.826
Oh my goodness!

21:29.746 --> 21:33.083
That's a hell of a welcome, damn it.

21:43.343 --> 21:44.636
I knew it.

21:45.304 --> 21:46.430
I don't think you did.

21:47.055 --> 21:48.265
Mind your age.

21:56.732 --> 21:58.150
Bet that stung, didn't it?

22:15.042 --> 22:17.210
Oh, so that's how you want to play it?

22:19.796 --> 22:21.298
Sweet! Got some loot.

22:42.069 --> 22:45.113
Come on, you fight with both hands.
You sure that one's enough?

22:47.074 --> 22:47.908
Whoa.

22:48.992 --> 22:50.118
I guess it is.

22:53.789 --> 22:55.040
Holy crap!

23:20.941 --> 23:23.276
Just stop already. I'm hungry.

23:23.777 --> 23:24.778
Why, you little…

23:25.654 --> 23:26.613
-Oh no.
-No!

23:54.057 --> 23:55.642
Eat your own food.

23:56.268 --> 23:57.561
I'm running out.

23:57.644 --> 24:02.232
At your age, eating this junk all the time
can't be good for you, old man.

24:03.483 --> 24:04.484
Clogged arteries.

24:04.568 --> 24:07.612
You're worried about my arteries,
but you never came to see me?

24:07.696 --> 24:10.824
Only because you and Min-kyu
ended things on really bad terms.

24:13.785 --> 24:17.122
I'm your pupil,
so I was really worried about you.

24:17.956 --> 24:18.790
I also felt bad.

24:19.749 --> 24:21.293
What's there to feel bad about?

24:21.376 --> 24:24.546
You were just an entry-level employee
at the time.

24:25.213 --> 24:28.842
A company executive handed a bloody knife
to the chairman,

24:30.552 --> 24:32.220
and the chairman accepted it.

24:33.388 --> 24:36.975
I retired instead of paying with my life,
so I should be grateful.

24:37.559 --> 24:40.812
What happened between you two?
You even started the company together.

24:41.980 --> 24:43.773
It was just a personal matter.

24:45.442 --> 24:46.776
You wouldn't get it.

24:54.576 --> 24:55.494
Hang on.

24:58.830 --> 25:00.582
Weren't you retired?

25:00.665 --> 25:03.919
So what's this douchey businessman doing
hanging around you?

25:04.002 --> 25:05.629
He looked sketchy as hell.

25:07.214 --> 25:10.133
You're gonna get investment from this punk
to start a company?

25:10.217 --> 25:13.845
He's just an immature kid
interested in this line of work.

25:15.013 --> 25:17.015
He's not in it for the money.

25:17.891 --> 25:19.726
Does that mean…

25:22.020 --> 25:24.773
you're testing the waters to return to MK?

25:27.150 --> 25:28.818
If you don't answer now,

25:28.902 --> 25:30.403
you're letting me slip away.

25:31.696 --> 25:33.406
Like you have anywhere to go.

25:33.490 --> 25:35.450
You really think I have nowhere to go?

25:37.410 --> 25:38.620
Seriously.

25:39.371 --> 25:40.205
Chairman.

25:40.705 --> 25:43.124
I'll treat you
with the utmost respect, okay?

25:44.084 --> 25:45.377
Hang on a minute.

25:47.295 --> 25:49.130
Sir, why didn't you act right away?

25:49.214 --> 25:50.799
The company's a mess right now.

25:50.882 --> 25:53.552
So they'd come looking for me.
Like you just did.

25:53.635 --> 25:55.512
Never expected any less.

25:55.595 --> 25:56.763
Speaking of which,

25:57.264 --> 25:59.766
I'd like to ask you a favor, Chairman.

26:00.475 --> 26:02.978
You remember Shin Jae-yi, don't you?

26:03.061 --> 26:04.813
She was the ace of our batch.

26:12.070 --> 26:13.738
You want to bring back someone

26:14.406 --> 26:15.740
who left on her own terms?

26:15.824 --> 26:17.284
I would've done the same.

26:17.784 --> 26:20.245
You picked me even though she beat me.

26:20.328 --> 26:21.955
The one we wanted

26:23.081 --> 26:24.666
was you, after all.

26:25.250 --> 26:26.209
"We"?

26:26.293 --> 26:27.419
Stop!

26:31.464 --> 26:32.424
What do you think?

26:33.091 --> 26:35.176
It seems the results are out.

26:37.262 --> 26:39.431
Why don't we head to the monitoring room?

26:42.851 --> 26:46.980
I heard Shin Jae-yi is always practicing.
It shows in her clean movements.

26:49.232 --> 26:51.693
See where Lee Han-ul's wooden knife hit?

26:51.776 --> 26:54.487
It's around the pancreas,
but it's not deep.

26:54.571 --> 26:56.948
Even a real blade would've grazed her.

26:57.032 --> 26:58.033
Shall we continue?

27:00.160 --> 27:03.747
He forced her to block with her right arm
because Shin Jae-yi is right-handed.

27:03.830 --> 27:04.706
But

27:05.457 --> 27:07.250
what if they were real blades?

27:11.254 --> 27:12.714
This wouldn't have happened.

27:13.340 --> 27:15.759
The skills gap will continue to grow.

27:15.842 --> 27:16.968
Shin Jae-yi

27:17.594 --> 27:19.971
will never catch up to Lee Han-ul.

27:23.642 --> 27:26.561
Oh, and see if you can teach him
your dual-wielding method.

27:27.062 --> 27:28.271
He's aggressive,

27:29.356 --> 27:31.566
so I think your style would suit him.

27:48.208 --> 27:50.710
It won't be easy for either of you.

27:52.712 --> 27:55.715
I won't allow Shin Jae-yi
under any circumstances.

27:58.134 --> 27:59.719
Seriously, what's the reason?

28:01.846 --> 28:03.973
Jae-yi seems to be avoiding you as well.

28:04.641 --> 28:06.017
If she's avoiding me,

28:06.976 --> 28:08.186
she must have her reasons.

28:09.437 --> 28:11.147
If you want, I can tell you.

28:16.027 --> 28:17.404
Nah, I'll pass.

28:25.370 --> 28:27.288
If you hadn't come to me,

28:28.707 --> 28:30.291
I'd have come to find you myself.

28:30.792 --> 28:33.753
The MK I'm rebuilding
will also need the next generation.

28:36.464 --> 28:38.216
Once my time is over…

28:40.760 --> 28:41.845
yours will come.

28:43.054 --> 28:43.972
You shouldn't

28:45.473 --> 28:47.100
waste that time on her.

28:50.437 --> 28:52.689
Who goes on a date in a place like this?

28:53.481 --> 28:54.816
How did you find this place?

28:54.899 --> 28:56.526
Your boss.

28:57.026 --> 28:59.529
He told me you bring your gear
on every date.

28:59.612 --> 29:02.699
So this is your boyfriend, huh?

29:03.199 --> 29:06.035
Is he giving you a hard time?
Want me to rough him up?

29:06.703 --> 29:07.912
You're so dead!

29:32.645 --> 29:33.938
-Where? Higher?
-Higher.

29:34.022 --> 29:35.023
Here?

29:35.106 --> 29:35.940
-Higher.
-Here?

29:36.024 --> 29:37.400
Hey, not there!

29:39.235 --> 29:41.946
I guess the old man's still going strong.

29:42.447 --> 29:44.574
He's not called "old man"
because he's old.

29:44.657 --> 29:45.784
It's because he's sly.

29:48.995 --> 29:52.665
I thought you weren't interested
in starting a business. So what changed?

29:53.958 --> 29:56.753
-Did the old man say anything?
-What would he say?

29:56.836 --> 29:58.213
I know how good I am,

29:58.713 --> 30:02.300
so it just felt like
I'd be doing the old man a favor again.

30:02.383 --> 30:05.345
Isn't that why you left
and started your own company?

30:05.428 --> 30:07.514
A company I ran into the ground.

30:08.014 --> 30:09.682
You didn't have me back then.

30:14.562 --> 30:15.980
You're one thing,

30:16.064 --> 30:17.899
but think about the kids too.

30:18.441 --> 30:20.109
They might lack brains,

30:20.193 --> 30:21.986
but not skill.

30:22.779 --> 30:24.447
Times have changed.

30:24.531 --> 30:26.491
Even you won't find an investor easily.

30:27.158 --> 30:28.076
Here!

30:32.789 --> 30:33.665
What do you think?

30:33.748 --> 30:36.876
Is that giving you confidence?

30:40.421 --> 30:41.297
What's wrong?

30:43.383 --> 30:44.384
Come on.

30:44.884 --> 30:48.513
How long are you gonna waste away
in that sorry-ass office?

30:49.013 --> 30:50.390
You need to be decisive.

30:51.307 --> 30:54.561
Want me to do it for you
if you can't bring yourself to?

30:55.770 --> 30:56.855
I understand.

30:57.897 --> 30:59.315
I figured this might happen.

30:59.399 --> 31:01.109
Given my current position,

31:01.609 --> 31:05.446
I don't think it's right for me
to hold onto you anymore.

31:07.657 --> 31:09.075
I'm sorry about this.

31:09.993 --> 31:12.370
Hey, don't say that.

31:14.038 --> 31:14.873
Go.

31:18.376 --> 31:19.794
I'll swing by now and then.

31:21.421 --> 31:22.255
Sure.

31:25.842 --> 31:27.218
-Su-min.
-Yes?

31:27.719 --> 31:30.847
Let's say there's a guy named A
and a girl named B.

31:30.930 --> 31:32.223
They've been bros for life.

31:32.307 --> 31:34.183
Except one of them is not a bro.

31:34.267 --> 31:36.352
The thing is, B said she had a boyfriend,

31:36.853 --> 31:38.688
but it turned out to be a lie.

31:42.525 --> 31:43.526
Why did she lie?

31:44.861 --> 31:45.987
It's like this.

31:46.070 --> 31:49.198
B knows all too well that A likes her,

31:49.282 --> 31:51.117
but it makes her uncomfortable.

31:51.200 --> 31:52.952
Why do you think that is?

31:53.036 --> 31:54.495
Because B also likes--

31:54.579 --> 31:57.373
It's because B doesn't see A as a man.

32:04.756 --> 32:07.133
For fuck's sake!
What's taking them so long?

32:11.554 --> 32:13.890
You can read him like an open book.

32:14.849 --> 32:16.517
Can't you put in a good word for me?

32:16.601 --> 32:18.645
I've still got some fight in me yet.

32:18.728 --> 32:21.648
Or just stay three more months.
That's all I ask, Jae-yi.

32:22.607 --> 32:23.524
Sir.

32:24.025 --> 32:25.318
I'm sorry.

32:25.818 --> 32:29.781
Can't you at least stay
until I find a replacement?

32:30.865 --> 32:34.077
Hey! Why the hell
are you guys moving so slowly?

32:34.160 --> 32:37.413
-Stuffing your face again?
-We were prepping the presentation.

32:37.497 --> 32:42.001
How did you land us such a major sponsor?

32:42.085 --> 32:44.504
We play Blood High School all the time.

32:45.338 --> 32:46.881
Blood… what?

32:50.927 --> 32:52.804
What's the take from real professionals?

32:52.887 --> 32:54.097
-Hello.
-Hello.

32:54.597 --> 32:57.392
That's the beta of Blood High School,
coming out soon.

32:57.892 --> 33:01.729
As a professional, I'd say
those characters would already be dead--

33:01.813 --> 33:04.315
But who'd play a game
that's just like real life?

33:04.399 --> 33:06.234
True. No one would play it.

33:06.317 --> 33:07.402
-Totally.
-Exactly.

33:08.236 --> 33:09.904
Wow, you're beautiful.

33:10.822 --> 33:13.241
I wanna scan you in 3D
and turn you into a game character.

33:17.453 --> 33:22.041
Last year, a total of 317,600 people died,

33:22.542 --> 33:27.588
which was an increase of 12,340 people,
or 4.2%, compared to the previous year.

33:27.672 --> 33:29.507
Of those, our company contributed…

33:29.590 --> 33:30.925
Should I keep going?

33:31.009 --> 33:31.968
Next slide.

33:34.053 --> 33:35.221
As for the ROI--

33:35.304 --> 33:37.140
Isn't that data from MK's peak?

33:37.807 --> 33:41.769
Corporate-style murder businesses
rarely turn a profit early on

33:41.853 --> 33:43.688
due to training and operating costs.

33:43.771 --> 33:45.314
That's enough profit talk.

33:45.398 --> 33:47.358
There's not much money in people's lives.

33:49.027 --> 33:51.404
Can I watch you work in person?

33:52.321 --> 33:55.116
-Excuse me?
-Seeing it in person would really help.

33:55.825 --> 33:57.410
Do you know why I'm doing this?

33:57.493 --> 34:00.204
I don't think we need to know that.

34:00.747 --> 34:04.584
Exactly. I'm not interested
in profits or numbers.

34:14.802 --> 34:15.970
I knew she was different.

34:17.096 --> 34:18.806
Your girlfriend, Mantis?

34:19.390 --> 34:21.893
Sorry. That was a little too personal.

34:21.976 --> 34:22.810
Now!

34:24.729 --> 34:25.980
Time for something fun?

34:28.399 --> 34:30.485
Name, Kim Dong-young.

34:30.568 --> 34:33.362
-He's 28, but a seven-year veteran…
-Not that dude.

34:33.446 --> 34:34.822
Pull up Jae-yi's chart.

34:39.202 --> 34:40.369
You've run a company.

34:40.453 --> 34:42.580
I think I've heard of that company before.

34:42.663 --> 34:43.581
Oh, right.

34:43.664 --> 34:46.167
It was an emerging player
during the industry's boom,

34:46.250 --> 34:48.211
but MK's monopoly brought it down.

34:48.294 --> 34:50.379
Wait, you were an intern at MK?

34:51.839 --> 34:53.299
That's ironic.

34:53.382 --> 34:54.634
You were big back then.

34:54.717 --> 34:57.470
So why did you end up
at some no-name company?

34:58.179 --> 35:00.932
She used to be the chairwoman
of a company,

35:01.015 --> 35:04.519
so small companies were likely hesitant
to hire someone of her caliber.

35:04.602 --> 35:07.605
And the big firms avoid her
because she tanked her last company?

35:08.106 --> 35:09.023
Not much use, then.

35:12.026 --> 35:15.029
I can personally vouch for her skills,

35:15.113 --> 35:16.572
so let's move on.

35:16.656 --> 35:18.741
How good is she anyway?

35:20.159 --> 35:21.786
What if she went up against you?

35:26.124 --> 35:28.292
Oh, sorry about that.

35:28.793 --> 35:31.254
I can't help being curious
about this kind of thing.

35:31.337 --> 35:34.715
Jae-yi, how would you fare
in a fight against Mantis?

35:38.052 --> 35:40.471
We're not fucking characters
in a fucking game.

35:42.265 --> 35:43.933
I'm someone who makes video games.

35:44.016 --> 35:45.059
I see.

35:45.560 --> 35:47.812
And I'm someone who kills people.

35:48.729 --> 35:51.983
Next time we meet, you're fucking dead.

35:53.484 --> 35:54.485
Hey!

35:55.444 --> 35:56.320
Let's go!

35:57.655 --> 36:00.449
"Fare"? What is this, a fucking bus ride?

36:03.286 --> 36:05.079
You can stay if you want.

36:06.831 --> 36:08.666
I can't help it when I'm curious.

36:08.749 --> 36:11.169
What are you doing? I said let's go.

36:11.669 --> 36:13.546
Your boyfriend is calling you.

36:18.426 --> 36:19.343
Sorry about that.

36:23.055 --> 36:25.641
Do you realize
what an opportunity he was for us?

36:25.725 --> 36:27.894
He's a prick
who'd never treat us like people.

36:27.977 --> 36:29.729
That punk was so disrespectful.

36:29.812 --> 36:32.106
Coming from someone
who kills for a living.

36:32.190 --> 36:33.316
This is work for us!

36:33.399 --> 36:35.776
You really wanna be treated like that
while working?

36:35.860 --> 36:36.694
Yes.

36:37.612 --> 36:38.446
What?

36:38.529 --> 36:40.281
I just want to do it.

36:40.781 --> 36:41.657
Work.

36:42.867 --> 36:44.243
I'll get you some work.

36:44.744 --> 36:45.661
I'm the Mantis.

36:45.745 --> 36:48.915
That was back when you were at MK.

36:48.998 --> 36:51.417
MK or not, I'm still the Mantis.

36:52.919 --> 36:55.087
-And what about us?
-You stay out of this.

36:55.171 --> 36:57.632
I get that you're the fucking Mantis!

36:58.132 --> 36:59.383
But what are we?

36:59.467 --> 37:00.718
Wanna get beat up again?

37:00.801 --> 37:02.220
Don't.

37:02.303 --> 37:03.554
You stop too, Dong-young.

37:03.638 --> 37:04.972
Stop what?

37:05.056 --> 37:06.432
To be honest,

37:07.558 --> 37:08.851
this is all because of you.

37:08.935 --> 37:10.019
What?

37:10.102 --> 37:13.189
Mantis is only sulking because of you.
Don't you fucking get it?

37:13.272 --> 37:14.398
Don't you guys see that?

37:14.941 --> 37:17.693
If you like her, just tell her.
Or go out with him.

37:17.777 --> 37:20.029
Stop acting like
a bunch of fucking children!

37:20.738 --> 37:23.824
Man, I'm so fucking over it.

37:27.245 --> 37:28.746
I'm going to go back up there.

37:28.829 --> 37:31.582
Why should I lose this chance
because of you two?

37:32.541 --> 37:34.919
Yang Su-min, Bboombye,
what are you guys gonna do?

37:37.463 --> 37:38.923
Fine. Live like that forever.

37:39.715 --> 37:40.967
Hey, Kim Dong-young!

37:41.050 --> 37:42.760
-Hey, Dong-young.
-Let go!

37:48.683 --> 37:50.351
Where are you going?

38:10.371 --> 38:12.999
Stop staring. You're embarrassing me.

38:13.499 --> 38:15.167
You're the one who called me out.

38:16.502 --> 38:17.461
Here.

38:19.171 --> 38:21.257
Whoa, this is…

38:21.340 --> 38:22.258
Yeah.

38:23.217 --> 38:25.386
What do you mean, "Yeah"? You idiot.

38:25.886 --> 38:28.180
Is that all you saved up working at MK?

38:29.515 --> 38:32.184
It did seem like you were splurging a lot.

38:32.268 --> 38:34.687
All the hotel stays, luxury goods,
and imported cars.

38:34.770 --> 38:36.772
I sold my car.

38:36.856 --> 38:38.566
And this is the replacement?

38:39.066 --> 38:40.067
Does it even run?

38:40.151 --> 38:42.320
How else would I have gotten here?

38:42.403 --> 38:45.072
Then go to the company that wants you
while it still runs.

38:45.156 --> 38:47.074
You don't have to do this for me.

38:53.122 --> 38:54.957
Was it really because of me?

39:00.921 --> 39:02.173
You knew too?

39:04.675 --> 39:06.469
I guess Su-min was right.

39:06.969 --> 39:09.263
You ignored it
because it was uncomfortable.

39:10.723 --> 39:13.351
It wasn't because of you. I did it for me.

39:13.434 --> 39:15.353
I'm the Mantis.

39:15.436 --> 39:17.688
I can't just go work
for some random company.

39:18.397 --> 39:21.442
I should start my own company
and make it the next MK.

39:22.026 --> 39:24.570
I won't make things uncomfortable for you,

39:25.071 --> 39:26.572
so help me out, okay?

39:28.783 --> 39:32.078
-Why should I?
-What do you mean "why"?

39:32.578 --> 39:34.580
Because you're good at what you do.

39:34.663 --> 39:35.915
You're not half bad.

39:37.958 --> 39:40.419
You're right.
I'm not half bad at what I do.

39:43.714 --> 39:44.924
This isn't me helping you.

39:45.424 --> 39:46.967
We're in this together, as equals.

39:47.635 --> 39:48.969
But I'll be the chairman.

39:50.846 --> 39:52.139
What did you expect?

39:53.182 --> 39:54.767
There won't be shows without me.

39:54.850 --> 39:56.560
You think you can bring them?

39:58.771 --> 40:02.233
I'll contact a few clients
I knew back at MK.

40:06.570 --> 40:07.571
Deal?

40:13.411 --> 40:14.328
Hey!

40:14.829 --> 40:16.372
I worked hard to get these.

40:16.455 --> 40:18.499
I'll assign them
based on your skill level,

40:18.582 --> 40:20.835
so make sure there are no mistakes.

40:20.918 --> 40:21.877
Yes, Chairman!

40:21.961 --> 40:22.920
"Chairman"?

40:23.003 --> 40:26.674
I know Dong-young's departure has us down,
but let's move forward.

40:26.757 --> 40:28.551
-Yes, Vice-Chairwoman!
-Vice-Chairwoman?

40:28.634 --> 40:32.138
See? You've got to be as quick
to catch on as Managing Director Yang.

40:32.221 --> 40:33.806
You're the managing director?

40:34.473 --> 40:37.685
Sir, is this all you scored?
I thought there'd be launch buzz.

40:37.768 --> 40:39.687
Work hard, and more jobs will follow.

40:39.770 --> 40:42.565
I have to take this level-A job.
This one's for Jae-yi.

40:43.149 --> 40:44.567
This one's for you, Ms. Yang.

40:44.650 --> 40:45.568
A level-D job?

40:45.651 --> 40:47.361
I'll take on this level-B.

40:47.862 --> 40:50.030
Take the level-C one too, Ms. Yang.

40:50.531 --> 40:51.407
What about me?

40:51.490 --> 40:52.741
You're crucial, Bboombye.

40:52.825 --> 40:55.369
Choose a spot for tonight's team dinner.

40:55.870 --> 40:56.704
What?

40:56.787 --> 40:58.080
I'm starving. Let's go.

40:58.164 --> 40:58.998
Yes, sir.

40:59.081 --> 41:01.750
And why am I still just Bboombye?

41:01.834 --> 41:03.627
Come on, Vice-Chairwoman. Let's go.

41:04.462 --> 41:06.589
Coming, sir!

41:07.089 --> 41:08.799
-What are we having?
-Budae-jjigae.

41:09.300 --> 41:10.551
We'll have pho.

41:12.428 --> 41:13.637
Easy! Just a bit.

41:14.889 --> 41:16.640
-Bottoms up!
-Let's go!

41:38.621 --> 41:41.248
Sir, what's our company called?

41:42.041 --> 41:43.417
The name!

41:44.585 --> 41:48.214
MANTIS COMPANY

42:00.976 --> 42:01.810
Let's go.

42:38.847 --> 42:41.141
Why are you slashing the price like that?

42:41.225 --> 42:43.269
What are people like us
supposed to live on?

42:43.352 --> 42:46.355
I have no choice if I'm to bring MK back.

42:46.855 --> 42:48.357
You think I'm enjoying this?

42:49.567 --> 42:51.944
I mean, even when we get a good show,

42:52.027 --> 42:55.030
we just don't have
reliable talent like you.

42:55.114 --> 42:56.949
Respected Chairman.

42:57.908 --> 43:01.036
Have you considered
outsourcing some of your shows to us?

43:01.120 --> 43:03.122
The ones MK likes to steer clear of.

43:03.622 --> 43:05.082
Even better if they're level-A.

43:05.165 --> 43:07.334
Wow, becoming chairman
has really matured you.

43:07.418 --> 43:09.587
The mighty Mantis has learned to beg.

43:09.670 --> 43:12.047
Are you going to help me or not?

43:12.965 --> 43:14.174
On one condition.

43:19.513 --> 43:21.056
I knew it.

43:22.808 --> 43:24.435
Since Min-kyu passed away,

43:25.019 --> 43:27.104
the number of unemployed has doubled.

43:27.605 --> 43:31.984
In other words,
the era of playing by the rules is over.

43:33.819 --> 43:37.781
That's why I hope to set things straight
before the year goes by.

43:39.158 --> 43:43.162
If you cooperate when the time comes,
things should go more smoothly.

43:43.245 --> 43:47.041
So you'll push the other companies down,
just as you have in the past?

43:47.708 --> 43:50.836
Now I understand why people are desperate
to join a large corporation.

43:50.919 --> 43:52.504
I get it now that I've left one.

43:52.588 --> 43:55.841
So why'd you leave
and make life harder for yourself?

43:55.924 --> 43:56.759
Huh?

44:06.101 --> 44:07.061
Out of the way.

44:29.583 --> 44:32.586
Why would you suddenly cancel the show?

44:32.670 --> 44:35.422
We already had the scenario ready to go.

44:35.506 --> 44:38.634
Please. I hear you've got a serious grudge
against the target.

44:38.717 --> 44:40.678
We'll make sure their death is painful.

44:40.761 --> 44:42.221
If you just trust us…

44:43.597 --> 44:45.224
Hello? Sir?

44:46.892 --> 44:47.851
Again?

44:47.935 --> 44:50.896
For fuck's sake. Level-C or not,
it was our first show in ages.

44:52.022 --> 44:53.065
Goddamn it!

44:53.148 --> 44:55.567
At least you still get to do fieldwork
now and then.

44:56.276 --> 44:58.862
How does a killer have eczema
on his hands?

44:59.947 --> 45:00.948
Jae-yi.

45:01.865 --> 45:03.909
Could you have a word with Mantis today?

45:03.992 --> 45:06.495
You're on company grounds.
Address him as Chairman.

45:06.578 --> 45:07.788
Who cares? It's just us.

45:07.871 --> 45:09.665
Are you saying Mantis isn't one of us?

45:10.165 --> 45:11.625
You're not calling him Chairman.

45:11.709 --> 45:14.920
Let's be honest.
I know you also have a lot of complaints.

45:15.003 --> 45:17.047
We're already short on work,

45:17.131 --> 45:19.383
and the chairman handles
most of the shows.

45:19.466 --> 45:20.342
What about me?

45:20.426 --> 45:21.301
What about you?

45:21.802 --> 45:23.721
That show came in for Han-ul.

45:23.804 --> 45:25.681
Don't like it? Score one yourselves.

45:25.764 --> 45:27.349
It's easier said than done.

45:27.433 --> 45:29.518
We're basically Mantis's one-man company.

45:29.601 --> 45:31.353
At least he's looking out for you--

45:35.774 --> 45:39.278
If I'd known it would end like this,
I'd have gone with Dong-young.

45:39.361 --> 45:41.196
Hey, Bboombye!

45:43.991 --> 45:46.910
Which one of you idiots
didn't recycle properly in the hallway?

45:47.578 --> 45:48.662
Welcome back, sir.

45:48.746 --> 45:49.580
It was him.

45:49.663 --> 45:51.248
Didn't you come from the scene?

45:51.749 --> 45:53.041
I had to land a show.

45:53.542 --> 45:54.543
This is yours, Jae-yi.

45:56.003 --> 45:58.338
Someone bailed on it,
so it needs to be done today.

45:58.839 --> 46:00.132
Today?

46:00.215 --> 46:02.092
It will be a breeze for you.

46:04.428 --> 46:05.387
Hey, Bboombye!

46:05.471 --> 46:07.181
Did you work on the scenario or not?

46:07.264 --> 46:08.515
You guys want to try this?

46:08.599 --> 46:09.767
-Yes.
-For real?

46:10.642 --> 46:12.102
What do you think you're doing?

46:12.603 --> 46:14.438
I entrusted you with that job.

46:15.105 --> 46:15.939
Huh?

46:16.690 --> 46:17.691
Chairman.

46:18.817 --> 46:20.235
I need to talk to you alone.

46:23.739 --> 46:25.365
We can't keep this up.

46:25.449 --> 46:28.035
To run a company,
we need to let the kids grow.

46:29.703 --> 46:32.289
-They've been complaining?
-It's not like that.

46:34.458 --> 46:35.626
You're the chairman.

46:36.710 --> 46:38.253
They're all counting on you.

46:41.340 --> 46:43.050
Yeah, I know.

46:44.218 --> 46:47.012
It's not like I don't pay them
or let them starve.

46:47.095 --> 46:48.764
Where can you find a boss like me?

46:49.932 --> 46:53.560
I cut my rates to land shows,
work my ass off, and split with everyone.

46:53.644 --> 46:56.897
Then stop working your ass off alone
and let us handle some shows.

46:57.397 --> 46:59.066
What if we screw up even one job?

46:59.566 --> 47:01.944
You wanna risk the company
right off the bat?

47:05.113 --> 47:08.283
Why did you even start a company
if you don't trust us?

47:09.910 --> 47:11.912
You only became Mantis

47:12.412 --> 47:14.456
because people at MK trusted you.

47:15.833 --> 47:18.085
Those kids are not on my level.

47:23.924 --> 47:25.008
Then how about me?

47:26.760 --> 47:27.678
What about you?

47:29.429 --> 47:31.849
Not you too. This is tiring as it is.

47:31.932 --> 47:34.059
You know I've been looking out for you.

47:39.231 --> 47:41.149
You promised not to make me uncomfortable.

47:42.359 --> 47:44.111
It makes me really uncomfortable

47:44.194 --> 47:46.738
when you blatantly look out for me
in front of the others.

47:51.243 --> 47:52.160
Okay.

47:52.870 --> 47:54.496
Looking out for you? Scratch that.

47:54.997 --> 47:55.914
Happy?

47:55.998 --> 47:57.916
Have you ever given me a level-A show?

47:59.585 --> 48:01.253
You are just an egomaniac

48:01.336 --> 48:04.298
who sees everyone,
including me, as beneath you.

48:06.800 --> 48:07.634
Fine.

48:09.011 --> 48:11.471
So you want me to give you
all the level-A shows?

48:13.223 --> 48:15.100
Not sinking into your thick skull?

48:16.059 --> 48:20.022
It disgusts me how you pretend to care
but look down on people.

48:24.151 --> 48:25.485
Damn it.

48:28.989 --> 48:30.198
So it disgusts you?

48:32.659 --> 48:33.493
Fine.

48:38.999 --> 48:39.833
Hey!

48:41.585 --> 48:44.504
You'd be screwed right now
if not for me. You know that?

48:45.255 --> 48:47.841
Isn't that why you ditched the boss
who had your back

48:47.925 --> 48:49.968
and joined a disgusting prick like me?

48:50.594 --> 48:52.721
What? Am I wrong?

48:52.804 --> 48:56.183
If you hate me looking down on you,
then outdo me and become the boss.

48:56.683 --> 48:58.810
What, want to go right now?

48:59.311 --> 49:00.145
Yeah?

49:03.440 --> 49:04.983
It must be nice being you.

49:06.652 --> 49:08.403
You're always right, after all.

49:32.844 --> 49:33.804
Is everything good

49:35.097 --> 49:36.306
between you and Jae-yi?

49:38.892 --> 49:41.561
I wonder why you keep talking
as if you know something.

49:43.689 --> 49:45.816
Oh my, speak of the devil.

49:49.569 --> 49:50.862
What is it, Vice-Chairwoman?

49:52.114 --> 49:53.115
It's done.

49:53.740 --> 49:55.450
I'll be heading straight home.

49:59.121 --> 50:00.372
Okay, good job.

50:00.872 --> 50:03.500
Have a safe trip home. See you--

50:05.627 --> 50:06.712
Hello?

50:07.504 --> 50:08.797
Still don't want to hear it?

50:09.673 --> 50:11.675
Why I won't allow Shin Jae-yi.

50:12.801 --> 50:15.554
If you're going to talk,
stop stalling and just tell me.

50:20.892 --> 50:23.311
What do you think happened
between Min-kyu and me?

50:26.690 --> 50:28.400
You said it was a personal matter.

50:44.166 --> 50:45.542
I've got customers on my tail.

50:56.178 --> 50:57.637
I was angry…

51:00.807 --> 51:02.142
that there was someone

51:02.851 --> 51:04.895
better than me by my side.

51:12.903 --> 51:14.279
Who are you guys?

51:16.114 --> 51:17.115
Never mind.

51:17.616 --> 51:18.950
Just don't tell me.

51:19.701 --> 51:22.120
I really feel like shit today, you see.

51:24.623 --> 51:26.208
Just don't run away.

51:28.794 --> 51:30.003
Not one of you pigs.

51:33.840 --> 51:35.759
Being talented is a gift.

51:37.511 --> 51:39.513
However, middling talent

51:40.263 --> 51:42.307
can actually be a curse instead.

51:42.390 --> 51:43.934
Why did you choose Han-ul over me?

51:44.017 --> 51:46.853
You'd have been cut down
if you'd fought with real blades.

51:49.439 --> 51:52.317
You seem clueless.
I guess that's to be expected.

51:53.610 --> 51:54.820
Someone told me

51:55.487 --> 51:58.740
you'd never catch up to Lee Han-ul.

51:58.824 --> 51:59.908
Shin Jae-yi

52:00.575 --> 52:02.536
will never catch up to Lee Han-ul.

52:05.580 --> 52:06.873
Never, you say?

52:07.582 --> 52:08.708
Never.

52:12.129 --> 52:13.922
Then let us fight with real blades.

52:15.173 --> 52:16.091
Let me fight

52:17.425 --> 52:19.136
Lee Han-ul with real blades.

52:20.428 --> 52:22.514
Do you even know what you're asking for?

52:22.597 --> 52:23.515
I do.

52:24.808 --> 52:27.018
Would I say it
if I didn't know what it meant?

52:27.769 --> 52:29.563
I don't dislike kids like you.

52:30.063 --> 52:31.565
That's why I'm contemplating.

52:32.065 --> 52:34.276
Whether I can go up against him or not?

52:34.359 --> 52:35.193
No.

52:39.447 --> 52:40.365
Whether to…

52:42.784 --> 52:44.619
let you go or not.

52:50.959 --> 52:52.669
Are you kicking me out?

52:54.296 --> 52:56.214
Just because I said I'd fight Han-ul?

52:56.715 --> 52:58.300
We can't ignore risks.

52:58.383 --> 53:00.969
The company has to protect
its greater assets.

53:03.972 --> 53:05.932
Kids like you always cause trouble.

53:10.770 --> 53:12.439
The chairman said that, didn't he?

53:14.065 --> 53:15.442
The word "never."

53:16.776 --> 53:18.737
And you accepted it

53:20.071 --> 53:21.573
like a fucking idiot.

53:23.700 --> 53:26.912
See? I knew you'd end up causing trouble.

53:57.400 --> 54:00.070
Did Jae-yi really say
she'd fight me with real blades?

54:03.865 --> 54:05.909
She's a lot like me.

54:08.745 --> 54:10.247
Particularly

54:10.330 --> 54:13.500
the way she fights tooth and nail to win.

54:14.000 --> 54:15.252
Just stop.

54:17.379 --> 54:18.755
It won't end well for you.

54:21.800 --> 54:23.009
Fuck you.

54:39.693 --> 54:41.278
You fucking shit!

54:45.699 --> 54:48.576
I knew she saw me as competition.

54:49.077 --> 54:51.788
But that doesn't mean
she wants to kill me.

54:52.998 --> 54:55.667
I didn't want to kill Cha Min-kyu either.

54:57.752 --> 55:00.588
You should've told me about this
a long time ago.

55:04.217 --> 55:07.095
I didn't think the two of you
would remain this close for so long.

55:09.472 --> 55:10.849
Once you leave the company…

55:12.892 --> 55:15.061
you should keep your distance from Han-ul.

55:15.895 --> 55:17.981
Being with someone you can never surpass…

55:21.776 --> 55:23.403
is just too cruel for you.

55:36.207 --> 55:37.625
In the end, I couldn't…

55:39.753 --> 55:42.088
distance myself from Cha Min-kyu either.

55:44.382 --> 55:45.842
I resented him,

55:47.218 --> 55:48.720
but I also admired him.

56:41.731 --> 56:42.690
Wait!

56:42.774 --> 56:43.608
Jae-yi!

56:44.109 --> 56:44.984
Jae-yi!

56:48.238 --> 56:50.281
How have you been?

56:50.365 --> 56:51.991
It's me, Dong-young.

57:02.419 --> 57:04.754
It wasn't Jae-yi who stayed by my side.

57:05.713 --> 57:07.674
I was the one who stayed by her side.

57:11.511 --> 57:13.596
If you insist on keeping her close,

57:13.680 --> 57:15.557
you need to let her know soon.

57:18.601 --> 57:20.186
The meaning of "never."

57:21.146 --> 57:23.690
If you're done playing around,
show yourself!

57:31.739 --> 57:34.325
I told you.
I can't help it when I'm curious.

57:37.495 --> 57:39.664
Is Mantis really better than you?

57:42.876 --> 57:44.794
Why still work for him?

57:45.920 --> 57:47.088
With those skills?

57:52.010 --> 57:54.137
-Jae-yi hasn't called, has she?
-Nope.

57:56.473 --> 57:57.807
-Jae-yi.
-Jae-yi!

57:57.891 --> 57:59.225
What the heck have you…

58:12.739 --> 58:14.032
Come here and eat.

58:14.115 --> 58:15.533
I don't feel like eating.

58:20.288 --> 58:21.539
Hey, you bastard.

58:22.040 --> 58:24.083
You drank again yesterday, didn't you?

58:24.167 --> 58:25.293
I didn't!

58:25.376 --> 58:27.295
I know you did. You should be working!

58:27.378 --> 58:28.796
I told you I didn't drink.

58:28.880 --> 58:31.216
Besides, I can't work if there's no work.

58:31.299 --> 58:33.676
So now you're talking back?
Step outside, you prick.

58:33.760 --> 58:35.345
-What now?
-Thinks he's big now.

58:35.428 --> 58:37.472
Just stop and let the kid eat.

58:42.685 --> 58:45.313
And where have you been all this time?

58:46.981 --> 58:48.107
I had something to do.

58:48.608 --> 58:49.943
And what was that?

58:50.026 --> 58:51.653
Just something.

58:53.112 --> 58:54.697
Just something? Like what?

58:56.324 --> 58:57.575
Didn't you hear me?

59:01.996 --> 59:03.998
Do I need to report everything to you?

59:04.082 --> 59:04.916
Yeah.

59:04.999 --> 59:06.000
Why is that?

59:07.752 --> 59:08.962
You really don't know?

59:10.213 --> 59:12.048
Because I'm your boss.

59:12.840 --> 59:14.217
I'm above you.

59:24.310 --> 59:25.311
Fine, then.

59:26.437 --> 59:27.647
Get your gear. Come out.

59:41.869 --> 59:43.621
Should we head outside too?

59:43.705 --> 59:45.373
They packed their real blades.

59:45.456 --> 59:47.750
Mantis told us to stay.
He said it would be okay.

59:47.834 --> 59:51.254
But how do you think Jae-yi will fare
against Han-ul now?

59:51.337 --> 59:53.423
She was training while Mantis goofed off.

59:53.506 --> 59:56.217
Are you worried about them
or just curious?

59:56.301 --> 59:58.261
Fuck it. I'm heading outside.

59:58.344 --> 59:59.178
Hey!

59:59.262 --> 01:00:00.930
Don't push yourself.

01:00:01.014 --> 01:00:02.974
I'll need some answers from you
after this.

01:00:03.474 --> 01:00:05.977
You're talking under the assumption
that you'll win.

01:00:06.060 --> 01:00:09.272
It's a fact, not an assumption.
And it'll never change.

01:00:41.721 --> 01:00:43.723
Holy shit. No fucking way.

01:00:43.806 --> 01:00:45.016
Man, that was scary.

01:00:48.603 --> 01:00:51.147
When did you get so good? Huh?

01:00:53.107 --> 01:00:55.193
Hey, I get it.

01:00:55.276 --> 01:00:56.736
Just stop already.

01:00:58.237 --> 01:00:59.113
Well, anyway,

01:00:59.947 --> 01:01:01.115
you're the chairwoman now.

01:01:01.199 --> 01:01:03.159
Let's get going now. They are waiting.

01:01:23.596 --> 01:01:24.639
Follow me if you want.

01:02:29.495 --> 01:02:32.373
See? An expert moves
on a whole different level.

01:02:32.457 --> 01:02:34.292
She really is different.

01:02:34.375 --> 01:02:38.087
These days, everyone has
someone they'd like to kill.

01:02:40.047 --> 01:02:41.674
A vicarious experience of killing.

01:02:48.556 --> 01:02:50.141
How are you guys doing?

01:02:51.517 --> 01:02:55.146
Well, since MK outsources to us,
we're pretty busy.

01:02:55.229 --> 01:02:59.066
If MK is outsourcing,
it must be cleaning up the unemployed.

01:03:01.110 --> 01:03:04.864
Hey, stop wasting your youth
and come join us.

01:03:04.947 --> 01:03:07.241
They have no future. We are the future.

01:03:07.325 --> 01:03:09.202
Get this. We're loaded with funding.

01:03:09.285 --> 01:03:11.662
Our chairwoman?
She's the biggest deal right now.

01:03:11.746 --> 01:03:14.040
The first-ever chairwoman in the industry!

01:03:14.123 --> 01:03:16.542
And Mantis has already hit rock bottom.

01:03:17.960 --> 01:03:19.629
I know you did that.

01:03:20.129 --> 01:03:20.963
Did what?

01:03:21.047 --> 01:03:24.050
You brought Mantis down
and set the stage for Jae-yi.

01:03:24.133 --> 01:03:26.260
Come on. As if I could pull that off.

01:03:26.344 --> 01:03:29.263
-Holy shit.
-That video you took that day…

01:03:29.347 --> 01:03:32.058
Fucking hell,
everyone in the industry has seen it.

01:03:32.558 --> 01:03:33.935
It wasn't me.

01:03:34.018 --> 01:03:36.646
Then did Jae-yi make you
upload that video?

01:03:37.772 --> 01:03:39.649
The chairwoman was against it as well.

01:03:42.360 --> 01:03:43.361
Right.

01:03:45.154 --> 01:03:48.324
What did I say?
In business, packaging is everything.

01:03:48.407 --> 01:03:49.909
Public relations and marketing.

01:03:49.992 --> 01:03:53.246
The rise of an unranked player
who took down Mantis, a top-ranked pro.

01:03:53.329 --> 01:03:54.288
And she's a woman.

01:03:55.081 --> 01:03:57.166
So I came up with a nickname for you.

01:03:57.250 --> 01:03:59.544
Did you know lizards eat mantises?

01:03:59.627 --> 01:04:00.920
Lizard?

01:04:01.838 --> 01:04:02.797
Killer name, no?

01:04:02.880 --> 01:04:05.383
I like Lizard. It really suits your image.

01:04:07.927 --> 01:04:09.095
I'll just use my name.

01:04:09.178 --> 01:04:10.096
Lizard.

01:04:11.264 --> 01:04:12.515
Let me cut to the chase.

01:04:13.224 --> 01:04:15.643
You know those rules MK set?

01:04:15.726 --> 01:04:18.145
Do we really have to follow them?

01:04:18.229 --> 01:04:19.981
Those rules may be fading now,

01:04:20.064 --> 01:04:23.109
but they're still the main justification
in this business.

01:04:23.192 --> 01:04:25.945
Unless you're running a corner store,
stick to principles.

01:04:26.028 --> 01:04:27.947
Justification and principles, huh?

01:04:28.447 --> 01:04:30.283
Think of it as a traffic light.

01:04:30.366 --> 01:04:33.160
Cha Min-kyu, who put up
the traffic lights, is already dead.

01:04:34.579 --> 01:04:35.663
I get it!

01:04:36.497 --> 01:04:37.957
Dokgo is still alive.

01:04:38.708 --> 01:04:40.167
Is he really that amazing?

01:04:41.836 --> 01:04:43.629
Would the Lizard deal no damage to him?

01:04:46.382 --> 01:04:48.342
So what you're saying is…

01:04:50.344 --> 01:04:51.929
it's not the rules,

01:04:52.430 --> 01:04:55.182
but the person using them
that's the problem, right?

01:04:55.808 --> 01:04:57.351
I just don't like that guy.

01:04:59.186 --> 01:05:00.605
He turned me down.

01:05:03.357 --> 01:05:04.400
So,

01:05:05.526 --> 01:05:07.695
don't turn me down, Lizard.

01:05:10.656 --> 01:05:12.825
Why did you bring this yourself?

01:05:13.326 --> 01:05:15.536
You could've just sent a subordinate.

01:05:16.037 --> 01:05:17.914
You shouldn't have.

01:05:17.997 --> 01:05:20.875
You've really let yourself go,
haven't you?

01:05:20.958 --> 01:05:22.376
Thanks anyway.

01:05:22.460 --> 01:05:25.004
Thanks for always dumping
the crappy jobs on us.

01:05:25.087 --> 01:05:26.589
Fine by me if you don't want it.

01:05:26.672 --> 01:05:28.007
Did I say I didn't want it?

01:05:28.090 --> 01:05:30.051
I said, "Thank you," didn't I?

01:05:30.551 --> 01:05:31.552
Make way.

01:05:32.845 --> 01:05:38.184
Do what I asked at the general assembly,
and the level-A shows are all yours.

01:05:38.267 --> 01:05:41.103
The Chinese Triads are at war these days.

01:05:42.271 --> 01:05:44.190
Well, I'm also from MK,

01:05:44.273 --> 01:05:46.108
so I'm all for having rules.

01:05:46.609 --> 01:05:49.737
But are you sure my cooperation
would make a difference in this situation?

01:05:52.156 --> 01:05:53.950
I saw that video as well.

01:05:55.618 --> 01:05:58.829
I've been hearing a lot
about Jae-yi's company lately.

01:05:59.330 --> 01:06:01.207
Word is, it's been growing fast.

01:06:01.874 --> 01:06:03.960
You want it, don't you?

01:06:04.460 --> 01:06:06.671
Too much greed
will give you a stomachache.

01:06:08.464 --> 01:06:10.299
Still not coming back to the company?

01:06:12.426 --> 01:06:15.346
Man, that's a seriously rough-looking mug.

01:06:17.056 --> 01:06:19.225
Who else is offering them shows?

01:06:19.308 --> 01:06:22.436
We've been blocking
all but a couple to avoid suspicion.

01:06:23.270 --> 01:06:24.897
Cut everything off now.

01:06:24.981 --> 01:06:25.982
Yes, sir.

01:06:30.319 --> 01:06:31.237
Han-ul.

01:06:31.904 --> 01:06:34.323
If you're not going to MK because of me,

01:06:34.407 --> 01:06:36.993
really, don't worry about me.

01:06:37.660 --> 01:06:38.577
Wanna try this?

01:06:38.661 --> 01:06:39.954
Seriously?

01:06:40.788 --> 01:06:43.666
-You'll take a level-D? Why would you--
-No one's forcing you.

01:06:44.166 --> 01:06:45.084
I'll try my best.

01:06:45.918 --> 01:06:48.254
You're sure you've got this, right?

01:06:48.754 --> 01:06:49.922
Managing Director Yang?

01:06:50.006 --> 01:06:53.426
Of course I do.
Just leave it up to me, sir.

01:06:54.343 --> 01:06:55.177
Fuck!

01:06:55.261 --> 01:06:56.804
-Ms. Yang!
-Huh?

01:06:57.304 --> 01:06:58.472
You said you got this!

01:06:58.556 --> 01:07:00.599
This is my scene. Why are you here?

01:07:00.683 --> 01:07:02.935
How could I not come when you're this bad?

01:07:03.728 --> 01:07:05.229
It's not over yet.

01:07:05.730 --> 01:07:07.773
Wait your turn, lad.

01:07:08.274 --> 01:07:09.984
I'm not done dealing with that lady.

01:07:10.067 --> 01:07:11.235
Ms. Yang!

01:07:11.318 --> 01:07:12.570
Damn it, seriously.

01:07:13.070 --> 01:07:15.489
Wrap this up in a minute, or you're fired.

01:07:43.934 --> 01:07:46.228
-Thirty seconds remaining.
-What?

01:07:46.312 --> 01:07:47.354
Crap.

01:07:49.023 --> 01:07:50.149
Screw this.

01:07:53.861 --> 01:07:55.196
Twenty seconds.

01:07:57.740 --> 01:07:58.574
Fifteen!

01:08:03.037 --> 01:08:04.038
Ten,

01:08:04.622 --> 01:08:05.498
nine,

01:08:06.499 --> 01:08:07.583
eight,

01:08:08.125 --> 01:08:09.335
seven,

01:08:10.252 --> 01:08:11.170
six,

01:08:11.712 --> 01:08:13.005
five,

01:08:13.631 --> 01:08:14.590
four,

01:08:15.132 --> 01:08:17.676
three, two,

01:08:18.469 --> 01:08:19.386
one!

01:08:25.726 --> 01:08:27.311
That was close.

01:08:30.147 --> 01:08:30.981
CLEANER

01:08:32.066 --> 01:08:33.734
Yes, this is Mantis.

01:08:34.401 --> 01:08:35.861
I need a cleanup, please.

01:08:37.196 --> 01:08:39.740
Man, level-B shows
are easier than I expected.

01:08:39.824 --> 01:08:42.493
I bet a level-A show
would be a cakewalk too.

01:08:43.202 --> 01:08:46.038
By the way,
are you really doing a level-D show?

01:08:47.289 --> 01:08:49.583
Hey, I'm still talking.
Where are you going?

01:08:50.334 --> 01:08:51.168
Sir.

01:08:51.669 --> 01:08:53.087
Yes, Mantis.

01:08:56.632 --> 01:08:58.968
-Take it.
-Come on, you shouldn't be doing this.

01:08:59.051 --> 01:09:00.094
Hey, it's fine.

01:09:05.641 --> 01:09:08.227
What are you doing?
We're deep in the red right now.

01:09:08.310 --> 01:09:11.438
Sure. Here. Grab something
for the general assembly.

01:09:13.023 --> 01:09:14.108
Thank you, sir.

01:09:18.821 --> 01:09:20.114
Isn't that Mantis?

01:09:27.580 --> 01:09:28.789
Hey, Mantis.

01:09:29.957 --> 01:09:31.542
Long time, no see.

01:09:32.126 --> 01:09:33.836
-I heard you started a company.
-Yes.

01:09:34.753 --> 01:09:38.132
But is she the only employee you have?

01:09:38.215 --> 01:09:39.925
Yes, she's enough.

01:09:40.593 --> 01:09:41.635
Aren't we late?

01:09:42.136 --> 01:09:43.679
Right, then.

01:09:43.762 --> 01:09:45.806
That short on work, huh?

01:09:45.890 --> 01:09:48.309
I guess the Mantis
isn't what he used to be.

01:09:49.977 --> 01:09:50.853
Damn it.

01:09:52.146 --> 01:09:54.565
Stop it. You're embarrassing me.

01:09:56.150 --> 01:09:57.610
Let's go.

01:10:03.532 --> 01:10:04.742
She's here.

01:10:07.286 --> 01:10:09.079
Oh my, Chairwoman Shin.

01:10:10.539 --> 01:10:13.417
I heard you gave yourself a nickname.
Lizard, was it?

01:10:13.500 --> 01:10:14.585
Long time, no see.

01:10:14.668 --> 01:10:15.711
I did no such thing.

01:10:15.794 --> 01:10:16.754
Let's get inside.

01:10:35.189 --> 01:10:36.607
As you all know,

01:10:37.733 --> 01:10:40.694
I distanced myself from this world
for a long time.

01:10:41.195 --> 01:10:42.446
People were curious

01:10:43.864 --> 01:10:47.368
why Dokgo returned.

01:10:48.661 --> 01:10:51.413
It's true that many colleagues
asked me to return…

01:10:53.666 --> 01:10:55.668
but I came back more out of duty.

01:10:56.710 --> 01:11:01.840
I had a sense of duty to protect
the legacy of the former chairman

01:11:02.591 --> 01:11:05.261
who made me retire.

01:11:06.387 --> 01:11:08.097
By legacy,

01:11:08.180 --> 01:11:11.475
do you mean the rules?

01:11:18.524 --> 01:11:20.401
I'm Shin Jae-yi from JB.

01:11:25.406 --> 01:11:27.574
I know you well, Chairwoman Shin.

01:11:27.658 --> 01:11:29.076
Anything you'd like to say?

01:11:29.576 --> 01:11:32.997
You're not here to preach,
and yet you're not getting to the point.

01:11:33.497 --> 01:11:37.084
Would you mind
if your junior summed up your speech?

01:11:37.668 --> 01:11:38.627
Please go ahead.

01:11:40.879 --> 01:11:43.716
"I heard you punks
haven't been following the rules lately."

01:11:43.799 --> 01:11:47.177
"So MK's stepping in like the old days

01:11:47.261 --> 01:11:50.139
to give the rule breakers
a proper walloping."

01:11:50.222 --> 01:11:51.515
Isn't that it?

01:11:53.309 --> 01:11:56.020
Thanks to the rules,
we do have fewer unemployed,

01:11:56.729 --> 01:12:00.024
but that also dried up work
for smaller companies,

01:12:00.649 --> 01:12:03.027
and their people broke the rules
to stay afloat.

01:12:03.110 --> 01:12:04.194
As a result,

01:12:04.945 --> 01:12:07.323
those companies all had to shut down.

01:12:08.032 --> 01:12:11.201
So you're suggesting we scrap the rules,

01:12:11.702 --> 01:12:13.579
bringing back an era of unemployment?

01:12:13.662 --> 01:12:16.582
I'm just saying
we should reconsider our approach

01:12:16.665 --> 01:12:19.251
if the results don't align
with our good intentions.

01:12:24.214 --> 01:12:25.841
Was that so hard to understand?

01:12:36.560 --> 01:12:41.231
I thought this was a general assembly,
not a boring debate tournament.

01:12:41.732 --> 01:12:44.360
Whatever, this stuff is over my head.

01:12:44.443 --> 01:12:46.153
Let's wrap up quickly and go home.

01:12:47.488 --> 01:12:48.405
Now!

01:12:49.239 --> 01:12:53.619
"I can no longer abide by the rules."

01:12:54.119 --> 01:12:54.953
Show your hands!

01:13:05.297 --> 01:13:08.550
"I want to scrap the sanctioned shows,

01:13:08.634 --> 01:13:10.886
even if the company takes a loss."

01:13:11.387 --> 01:13:15.557
"If the pay's good enough,
I'm willing to be a child-killing animal."

01:13:16.100 --> 01:13:17.434
Let's see your hands.

01:13:23.857 --> 01:13:24.691
Settled?

01:13:25.984 --> 01:13:28.529
-We're done.
-I never said not to follow the rules.

01:13:28.612 --> 01:13:31.156
We must follow the rules,
or we will be punished.

01:13:31.740 --> 01:13:32.574
What?

01:13:33.158 --> 01:13:34.868
But why does…

01:13:37.287 --> 01:13:38.414
MK get to punish them?

01:13:42.042 --> 01:13:43.669
Last year's Gil Boksoon incident…

01:13:44.670 --> 01:13:47.005
Five of our colleagues died
in a single night.

01:13:47.673 --> 01:13:50.926
Then MK ran an internal investigation
and ended it abruptly.

01:13:51.009 --> 01:13:52.553
On top of that,

01:13:52.636 --> 01:13:55.722
the head of a company
and MK's director died in the process.

01:13:56.390 --> 01:13:57.891
And lastly…

01:14:01.728 --> 01:14:05.524
even the true chairman of MK,
who made those rules, ended up dead.

01:14:10.320 --> 01:14:12.573
Does MK still have the right
to punish anyone?

01:14:16.368 --> 01:14:18.162
Then who else would do it?

01:14:19.288 --> 01:14:23.834
Punishment's only effective
when delivered by the strongest.

01:14:25.961 --> 01:14:28.255
Why not let me give it a go?

01:14:28.839 --> 01:14:30.757
Can you really live up to those words?

01:14:30.841 --> 01:14:32.009
Yes.

01:14:35.512 --> 01:14:37.139
Then would you mind

01:14:37.222 --> 01:14:39.516
if I tested you right here, right now?

01:14:42.227 --> 01:14:43.061
By all means.

01:14:51.653 --> 01:14:52.571
Chairman!

01:14:53.739 --> 01:14:54.865
Chairman!

01:14:56.283 --> 01:14:57.117
Chairman.

01:14:57.201 --> 01:14:59.745
What the hell were you two thinking?

01:15:00.871 --> 01:15:03.123
Open your eyes, Han-ul.

01:15:04.458 --> 01:15:06.627
It makes me tear up.

01:15:07.586 --> 01:15:10.422
-Your friend spared you the shame.
-Han-ul. Chairman!

01:15:11.131 --> 01:15:12.466
Open your eyes, Chairman.

01:15:12.549 --> 01:15:14.384
Who was spared from embarrassment?

01:15:14.468 --> 01:15:17.012
Han-ul! Wake up!

01:15:17.846 --> 01:15:20.557
This is driving me crazy. Han-ul!

01:15:21.183 --> 01:15:22.684
Get up, please.

01:15:25.187 --> 01:15:26.563
Seriously, what do I do?

01:15:27.147 --> 01:15:28.273
You can get up now.

01:15:31.777 --> 01:15:33.320
It hurts there!

01:15:34.446 --> 01:15:35.989
That hurts, damn it.

01:15:36.490 --> 01:15:37.950
You did that on purpose, huh?

01:15:48.377 --> 01:15:50.587
No, that's all.

01:15:50.671 --> 01:15:53.423
She was really out for blood today.

01:15:53.507 --> 01:15:55.092
If she keeps this up…

01:15:55.592 --> 01:15:56.677
Understood.

01:15:56.760 --> 01:15:58.679
…I won't be able to let it slide.

01:15:59.513 --> 01:16:01.723
You know that's not Jae-yi's intention.

01:16:01.807 --> 01:16:04.101
That immature idiot's curiosity
is to blame.

01:16:04.184 --> 01:16:05.102
Then what?

01:16:06.311 --> 01:16:08.230
Wait, that's all?

01:16:10.440 --> 01:16:12.150
Okay for now.

01:16:12.234 --> 01:16:14.152
I did my part, so keep your word.

01:16:14.236 --> 01:16:15.696
All the level-A shows.

01:16:15.779 --> 01:16:17.406
Done with everything I gave you?

01:16:17.489 --> 01:16:18.991
I finished one,

01:16:19.074 --> 01:16:22.286
and I'll finish the other
by the end of the day.

01:16:22.369 --> 01:16:24.830
Let's talk after you've finished that one.

01:16:27.124 --> 01:16:29.626
-Did something interesting happen?
-Oh yes.

01:16:31.211 --> 01:16:32.546
Come here for a second.

01:16:37.509 --> 01:16:38.927
What now?

01:16:39.553 --> 01:16:40.721
Hey.

01:16:41.221 --> 01:16:43.223
It's okay. You won't die.

01:16:43.724 --> 01:16:45.100
Hey, wait!

01:16:46.310 --> 01:16:49.730
Does this mean we're up against MK now?

01:16:51.064 --> 01:16:53.775
Isn't it a bit too soon?

01:16:53.859 --> 01:16:55.527
We're just a new company.

01:16:55.611 --> 01:16:58.238
I accepted this risk
the moment I joined Benjamin.

01:16:59.323 --> 01:17:03.076
We just need to play the obedient dog
until we're strong enough to face MK.

01:17:03.994 --> 01:17:04.995
What do you mean?

01:17:05.078 --> 01:17:07.664
I'll settle my score with Dokgo
when I choose,

01:17:08.165 --> 01:17:09.291
on my own terms.

01:17:10.917 --> 01:17:14.087
Before that, I'll cut off the hand I took.

01:17:15.547 --> 01:17:18.008
Are you saying you'll betray Mr. Jo?

01:17:19.718 --> 01:17:21.261
It wouldn't be the first time.

01:17:39.988 --> 01:17:41.114
Oh my.

01:18:01.968 --> 01:18:02.803
I see.

01:18:04.763 --> 01:18:06.264
I knew

01:18:06.848 --> 01:18:08.141
this day would come.

01:18:08.225 --> 01:18:09.476
Right?

01:18:09.976 --> 01:18:12.771
You should've just retired
when you became unemployed.

01:18:13.355 --> 01:18:14.815
This breaks my heart.

01:18:29.454 --> 01:18:30.706
Make it quick.

01:18:32.582 --> 01:18:33.709
Before I die,

01:18:35.085 --> 01:18:36.753
let me see your skills.

01:18:47.139 --> 01:18:49.766
Why shut your eyes
if you wanna see my skills?

01:18:58.525 --> 01:18:59.860
Just open that up for me.

01:19:08.076 --> 01:19:10.162
I'll be taking the torso.

01:19:10.746 --> 01:19:12.289
We just need to send the head.

01:19:12.372 --> 01:19:14.624
Are you acting out of pity or guilt?

01:19:14.708 --> 01:19:17.294
Quick, change his clothes.
We're short on time.

01:19:17.377 --> 01:19:19.212
This is a violation of the rules.

01:19:20.172 --> 01:19:21.965
This will also cause you trouble.

01:19:22.549 --> 01:19:25.927
MK wouldn't even bother paying attention
to a show like this.

01:19:31.516 --> 01:19:33.477
Fucking hell. Right to the end.

01:19:36.897 --> 01:19:39.441
What, even human lives are ranked now?

01:19:41.568 --> 01:19:42.694
Then what am I?

01:19:44.780 --> 01:19:45.781
Ranked C?

01:19:46.865 --> 01:19:48.241
Fucking hell.

01:19:49.659 --> 01:19:50.744
Just kill me.

01:19:51.912 --> 01:19:53.038
What are you doing?

01:19:53.121 --> 01:19:55.415
Just fucking kill me, okay?

01:19:57.501 --> 01:19:58.543
What's wrong?

01:19:58.627 --> 01:20:02.506
You thought I'd bow and thank you
for saving my worthless life?

01:20:04.591 --> 01:20:07.219
Why blame someone else
for ruining your own life?

01:20:08.011 --> 01:20:09.930
Blame your own incompetence.

01:20:20.106 --> 01:20:22.651
You rank D, at best.

01:20:23.235 --> 01:20:24.861
See? Happy?

01:20:27.072 --> 01:20:29.574
Besides, you don't really want to die.

01:20:29.658 --> 01:20:31.785
Then you'd have at least put up a fight.

01:20:43.338 --> 01:20:44.923
Go somewhere no one knows you,

01:20:46.299 --> 01:20:48.301
and live out your days in obscurity.

01:20:59.938 --> 01:21:01.857
I could've done it if you had asked.

01:21:04.317 --> 01:21:05.485
I know.

01:21:06.403 --> 01:21:10.949
OLD MAN DOKGO

01:21:15.453 --> 01:21:17.455
Hey, old man.

01:21:17.956 --> 01:21:19.374
I mean, Chairman.

01:21:19.916 --> 01:21:21.710
I was just about to call you.

01:21:22.252 --> 01:21:24.087
Everything has been wrapped up.

01:21:29.009 --> 01:21:29.885
What about Jae-yi?

01:21:34.931 --> 01:21:36.850
She sent me a message.

01:21:36.933 --> 01:21:38.059
What kind of message?

01:21:48.528 --> 01:21:50.488
You're not going to accept it, are you?

01:21:50.572 --> 01:21:51.990
Since a junior sent me this,

01:21:52.908 --> 01:21:55.035
it's only right
that I respond as a senior.

01:21:55.118 --> 01:21:56.369
Hey, that's…

01:21:57.037 --> 01:21:59.205
What are you talking about, old man?

01:21:59.915 --> 01:22:01.833
If you interfere,
I won't let you off either.

01:22:01.917 --> 01:22:05.086
That fucking kid Benjamin
is playing both of you right now!

01:22:05.587 --> 01:22:07.631
I'm playing along, not getting played.

01:22:07.714 --> 01:22:09.466
Okay, listen to me. I'll…

01:22:09.549 --> 01:22:10.550
Just listen.

01:22:10.634 --> 01:22:13.219
I'll let you settle this
without spilling a drop of blood.

01:22:14.429 --> 01:22:15.555
How would you do that?

01:22:17.098 --> 01:22:18.683
If I force Shin Jae-yi to her knees

01:22:19.643 --> 01:22:21.728
and make her take back the knife,
is that enough?

01:22:23.980 --> 01:22:26.441
And how's that going to help me?

01:22:29.361 --> 01:22:30.195
It will.

01:22:31.655 --> 01:22:32.906
Mantis

01:22:33.949 --> 01:22:35.492
will be returning to MK.

01:22:42.749 --> 01:22:45.293
Settle this within 24 hours.

01:23:10.485 --> 01:23:14.489
LEE HAN-UL

01:23:20.078 --> 01:23:21.913
The number you have dialed…

01:23:33.425 --> 01:23:35.051
The number you have dialed…

01:23:48.481 --> 01:23:49.691
Su-min.

01:23:49.774 --> 01:23:50.608
Yes.

01:23:51.526 --> 01:23:53.778
Send out funeral notices by text.

01:24:05.415 --> 01:24:08.251
Chairwoman Shin, glad you made it on time.

01:24:08.334 --> 01:24:09.753
Have you been well?

01:24:09.836 --> 01:24:10.962
Go inside.

01:24:16.676 --> 01:24:17.927
We need to talk.

01:24:25.769 --> 01:24:27.437
About Bae-soo…

01:24:29.689 --> 01:24:30.690
I did him in.

01:24:33.943 --> 01:24:36.362
He lived off unsanctioned shows
after his company closed.

01:24:44.370 --> 01:24:46.081
Why are you telling me this?

01:24:48.208 --> 01:24:49.042
What for?

01:24:49.709 --> 01:24:51.044
Are you saying it's my fault?

01:24:54.964 --> 01:24:56.758
Actually, it was my fault.

01:25:02.847 --> 01:25:04.390
Sending the old man the knife

01:25:06.226 --> 01:25:07.685
wasn't your idea, was it?

01:25:10.897 --> 01:25:12.065
I sent it to him.

01:25:15.568 --> 01:25:16.778
Take it back.

01:25:19.280 --> 01:25:20.156
Why should I?

01:25:20.240 --> 01:25:22.909
Because I don't want to go
to your funeral.

01:25:30.875 --> 01:25:33.378
Do I have any reason left
to listen to you?

01:25:36.965 --> 01:25:38.466
Aren't I above you now?

01:25:42.345 --> 01:25:44.722
Did you really hate
me being above you that much?

01:25:45.223 --> 01:25:46.474
Is that why…

01:25:49.018 --> 01:25:50.520
you wanted to kill me?

01:25:55.275 --> 01:25:56.484
Is that what Dokgo said?

01:26:01.489 --> 01:26:03.116
I couldn't fucking stand you…

01:26:05.368 --> 01:26:06.452
or myself.

01:26:10.582 --> 01:26:13.001
Why was it always you and never me?

01:26:15.170 --> 01:26:19.007
And why did this clueless prick
stay by my side

01:26:19.090 --> 01:26:20.925
like a fucking idiot?

01:26:22.719 --> 01:26:26.347
If you hated me staying by your side
like a fucking idiot that much…

01:26:28.349 --> 01:26:30.185
why didn't you just get lost?

01:26:32.228 --> 01:26:33.605
That would be running away.

01:26:36.149 --> 01:26:38.276
I didn't want to run away from you.

01:26:41.779 --> 01:26:44.616
I extended my hand to you,
even after I lost.

01:26:45.491 --> 01:26:46.326
You know that?

01:26:46.409 --> 01:26:49.829
One should only grab hands
from the same height.

01:26:53.291 --> 01:26:55.293
We're past convincing each other
with words, huh?

01:27:03.968 --> 01:27:05.261
Come outside.

01:27:09.474 --> 01:27:10.725
Whoa, hey.

01:27:10.808 --> 01:27:12.977
What's going on?

01:27:13.061 --> 01:27:14.020
What is this?

01:27:14.103 --> 01:27:15.313
What the…

01:27:15.855 --> 01:27:16.689
Good God.

01:27:17.190 --> 01:27:18.441
Oh my.

01:27:18.524 --> 01:27:19.734
Thank you all so much

01:27:20.443 --> 01:27:22.820
for attending my funeral.

01:27:22.904 --> 01:27:24.072
What the…

01:27:24.155 --> 01:27:25.073
What's…

01:27:28.910 --> 01:27:29.911
It's been a while.

01:27:31.412 --> 01:27:32.747
Boss.

01:27:35.291 --> 01:27:37.710
There's no need to cancel the funeral.

01:27:38.670 --> 01:27:40.255
I've already contacted MK.

01:27:41.422 --> 01:27:43.091
They'll send someone else for me.

01:27:43.174 --> 01:27:44.634
What the hell are you doing?

01:27:46.052 --> 01:27:48.012
I thought about what you said.

01:27:52.225 --> 01:27:53.309
I may not be

01:27:54.394 --> 01:27:56.396
someone you need,

01:27:57.063 --> 01:27:58.189
but I realized

01:27:59.399 --> 01:28:00.650
I could be someone

01:28:01.484 --> 01:28:02.777
you don't want around.

01:28:25.758 --> 01:28:27.051
Step outside, Su-min.

01:28:30.930 --> 01:28:33.141
You really screwed up big-time.

01:28:33.224 --> 01:28:36.185
You know I can't cover this up
for you, don't you?

01:28:36.811 --> 01:28:37.895
Right.

01:28:41.858 --> 01:28:44.027
It's a complete mess.

01:28:45.361 --> 01:28:46.779
It's the one Jae-yi sent me.

01:28:47.989 --> 01:28:49.657
I couldn't prepare another one.

01:28:50.867 --> 01:28:52.660
I have to take this, don't I?

01:28:59.125 --> 01:29:00.209
I'm only

01:29:01.336 --> 01:29:03.796
showing you respect
because you're the Mantis.

01:29:07.467 --> 01:29:09.302
When are you meeting with Jae-yi?

01:29:12.388 --> 01:29:13.931
I'll see her before I see you.

01:29:19.312 --> 01:29:21.356
Let me know
once you have a time and place.

01:29:46.756 --> 01:29:47.965
God, it's freezing.

01:29:51.177 --> 01:29:54.472
How did it feel
sending the knife to Min-kyu?

01:29:56.974 --> 01:29:59.310
Not so different from how you feel now.

01:29:59.811 --> 01:30:01.771
Both sender and recipient feel like crap.

01:30:03.064 --> 01:30:06.359
You're bound to get the bloody knife
from the one closest to you.

01:30:15.243 --> 01:30:16.327
Fucking hell!

01:30:31.717 --> 01:30:34.053
Do you want to kill her or protect her?

01:30:40.893 --> 01:30:41.936
That's right.

01:30:42.979 --> 01:30:45.064
If you want to protect something,
protect it.

01:30:47.900 --> 01:30:49.694
Jae-yi.

01:30:54.657 --> 01:30:55.783
But

01:30:56.325 --> 01:30:58.369
that sly senior of yours is really strong.

01:30:58.953 --> 01:31:00.580
What did you just say?

01:31:00.663 --> 01:31:03.916
I said I sent the knife
you gave me to Jae-yi.

01:31:04.000 --> 01:31:04.876
TOMORROW AT 5, MK

01:31:15.136 --> 01:31:17.263
Things will get messy no matter what I do,

01:31:18.514 --> 01:31:20.641
so I decided to mess things up a little.

01:32:02.975 --> 01:32:04.393
Don't forget your car keys.

01:32:04.894 --> 01:32:06.479
You can have that junker.

01:32:07.438 --> 01:32:10.233
Why talk like you won't see me again?
You'll be here tomorrow.

01:32:10.816 --> 01:32:11.984
I'm going.

01:32:13.694 --> 01:32:14.987
Now that I think about it,

01:32:16.155 --> 01:32:18.324
B might have liked A too.

01:32:22.411 --> 01:32:23.454
What are you saying?

01:32:25.581 --> 01:32:28.042
I'm talking about A and B,
the lifelong bros.

01:32:30.336 --> 01:32:31.212
That's just

01:32:32.588 --> 01:32:35.716
what C, who used to have
a crush on A, thinks anyway.

01:32:46.102 --> 01:32:47.186
See you tomorrow.

01:32:57.113 --> 01:32:59.240
LEE HAN-UL

01:33:04.287 --> 01:33:05.371
Are you on your way?

01:33:06.998 --> 01:33:08.165
This is pointless.

01:33:08.666 --> 01:33:11.168
I'm just trying to boost our odds.

01:33:11.836 --> 01:33:15.131
I'll wait on the first floor.
Let's talk before heading upstairs.

01:33:28.686 --> 01:33:30.146
He's waiting on the upper level.

01:33:38.070 --> 01:33:39.363
Aren't you going up?

01:33:40.698 --> 01:33:42.033
There's still some time left.

01:33:43.159 --> 01:33:45.453
Chairwoman Shin Jae-yi
has already gone up.

01:33:48.372 --> 01:33:49.457
Damn it.

01:34:06.474 --> 01:34:07.391
What's wrong?

01:34:09.060 --> 01:34:10.561
Not seeing who you came for?

01:34:12.563 --> 01:34:16.233
Thought you'd have a shot
if it was a two-on-one fight?

01:34:16.734 --> 01:34:17.943
Could be for the best.

01:34:19.403 --> 01:34:20.529
How so?

01:34:23.407 --> 01:34:25.409
I'll end you before Shin Jae-yi arrives.

01:34:42.218 --> 01:34:43.344
End me?

01:34:46.389 --> 01:34:49.767
Let me explain how I'll proceed.

01:34:51.268 --> 01:34:54.063
I'll lunge at her
the moment the door opens.

01:34:56.816 --> 01:34:58.901
If you find an opening against me,

01:34:59.735 --> 01:35:01.696
you simply go for it.

01:35:17.920 --> 01:35:18.754
What's wrong?

01:35:19.547 --> 01:35:20.840
It bothers you that much?

01:35:26.554 --> 01:35:28.347
What are you doing? Shin Jae-yi!

01:35:31.016 --> 01:35:32.977
Do you understand, Chairwoman Shin?

01:35:33.060 --> 01:35:35.229
This isn't a two-on-one fight.

01:35:36.272 --> 01:35:39.066
It's me and Mantis, one-on-one,
with his weakness in play.

01:35:40.025 --> 01:35:41.569
He's trying to provoke you.

01:35:41.652 --> 01:35:43.112
Don't fall for it.

01:35:47.742 --> 01:35:49.368
Stay focused!

01:35:55.291 --> 01:35:56.709
What the hell are you doing?

01:35:56.792 --> 01:35:58.210
Fuck off.

01:35:58.919 --> 01:36:00.337
No one agreed to a two-on-one.

01:36:00.838 --> 01:36:02.882
This is a one-on-one-on-one.

01:36:10.222 --> 01:36:11.515
Are you for real?

01:36:17.271 --> 01:36:18.856
It's been a while, Shin Jae-yi.

01:36:45.090 --> 01:36:46.467
I told you, didn't I?

01:36:47.802 --> 01:36:49.553
Stop wasting your time on her.

01:37:05.778 --> 01:37:07.071
Move!

01:39:03.854 --> 01:39:06.315
All that work just to get in one blow.

01:39:15.324 --> 01:39:16.659
Now it's even.

01:39:17.576 --> 01:39:19.787
Better this than fighting with a weakness.

01:39:20.412 --> 01:39:22.498
It seems Jae-yi is smarter than you.

01:39:24.583 --> 01:39:26.168
But this won't change anything.

01:39:28.087 --> 01:39:31.465
Old man, I really wasn't going to do this.

01:39:36.428 --> 01:39:37.930
But I'll just show you.

01:39:42.768 --> 01:39:44.645
The meaning of "never."

01:39:45.771 --> 01:39:46.939
Take a good look.

01:40:11.130 --> 01:40:12.506
Take this seriously!

01:40:14.758 --> 01:40:16.510
Why don't you make me?

01:40:46.206 --> 01:40:47.666
Don't look at me like that.

01:40:52.087 --> 01:40:53.297
Retire.

01:40:56.967 --> 01:40:58.427
We'll end it at that.

01:41:15.944 --> 01:41:17.071
Retire.

01:41:36.215 --> 01:41:38.342
I won't do it again.

01:41:41.929 --> 01:41:44.014
I don't want to kill you either.

01:41:49.812 --> 01:41:51.980
That's the problem with you.

01:41:54.191 --> 01:41:57.236
This won't end until one of us dies.

01:43:13.854 --> 01:43:15.439
Did you have to do that?

01:43:20.277 --> 01:43:22.112
You pity people…

01:43:24.865 --> 01:43:27.117
and it only makes them miserable.

01:43:31.413 --> 01:43:33.790
That hand you offered me back then
was pity too.

01:43:35.876 --> 01:43:37.836
Thought I wouldn't know you let me win?

01:43:47.262 --> 01:43:48.972
I regret it sometimes.

01:43:53.143 --> 01:43:54.978
Maybe I should have…

01:43:56.980 --> 01:43:59.191
just played dumb and taken your hand.

01:44:03.403 --> 01:44:05.030
What would've happened then?

01:44:16.541 --> 01:44:17.376
No.

01:44:22.464 --> 01:44:23.715
You did the right thing.

01:44:33.100 --> 01:44:34.643
You got everything you wanted.

01:44:41.316 --> 01:44:42.276
You did great.

01:46:08.737 --> 01:46:10.739
It's a cruel world out there.

01:46:11.490 --> 01:46:13.492
The weak are eaten by the strong,

01:46:14.034 --> 01:46:16.036
and the strong prey on the weak.

01:46:17.496 --> 01:46:20.290
How should we live in a world like this?

01:46:20.374 --> 01:46:22.209
We should take after the world.

01:46:23.251 --> 01:46:25.128
We must become both cruel and powerful.

01:46:25.212 --> 01:46:28.048
Then what do you think
the first condition of power is?

01:46:28.548 --> 01:46:29.383
Authority!

01:46:30.217 --> 01:46:31.551
Wealth!

01:46:31.635 --> 01:46:33.178
Our parents' wealth!

01:46:34.971 --> 01:46:36.848
That last one does have a point.

01:46:36.932 --> 01:46:38.975
Wealth and authority.

01:46:39.476 --> 01:46:42.687
They're not conditions for power
but trophies of it.

01:46:43.772 --> 01:46:45.941
I believe the first condition

01:46:47.526 --> 01:46:48.777
is timing.

01:46:50.529 --> 01:46:55.534
In a world where friends turn into enemies
and enemies into friends,

01:46:55.617 --> 01:46:59.746
we must sometimes be hunted
and sometimes hunt.

01:47:00.247 --> 01:47:02.207
Sometimes we must put up a fight

01:47:03.208 --> 01:47:04.418
and know when to avoid one.

01:47:05.710 --> 01:47:08.130
Knowing the right time to strike

01:47:09.631 --> 01:47:10.841
is where success begins.

01:47:14.928 --> 01:47:16.972
Nice speech, sir.

01:47:17.055 --> 01:47:19.850
I hope my heartfelt message
reaches the youth.

01:47:21.685 --> 01:47:22.936
That was great.

01:47:23.770 --> 01:47:24.855
How did you like it?

01:47:25.355 --> 01:47:26.398
It really resonated.

01:47:26.481 --> 01:47:28.817
Especially the part
about timing the strike.

01:47:28.900 --> 01:47:30.735
Of course. That was my point.

01:47:30.819 --> 01:47:32.529
Is the MK takeover going smoothly?

01:47:32.612 --> 01:47:34.656
Yes. It will be completed soon.

01:47:34.739 --> 01:47:37.868
Congratulations.
I picked the right person for the job.

01:47:37.951 --> 01:47:39.411
Raising you has been fun.

01:47:39.494 --> 01:47:40.912
I owe it all to you, sir.

01:47:40.996 --> 01:47:42.664
Give me a status report tomorrow.

01:47:44.249 --> 01:47:45.167
Take care, sir.

01:47:54.009 --> 01:47:55.469
When is our time to strike?

01:47:57.262 --> 01:47:58.096
Soon.

01:48:05.145 --> 01:48:05.979
Hang on.

01:48:09.941 --> 01:48:10.817
I gave the job

01:48:11.318 --> 01:48:13.695
to a company desperate for a level-A show.

01:48:18.408 --> 01:48:20.452
What up, you fucking douche?

01:48:20.535 --> 01:48:23.580
I told you you'd be dead
the next time we met, didn't I?

01:51:28.765 --> 01:51:33.978
MANTIS

01:51:34.062 --> 01:51:39.067
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
